# getAnisotropicDimension
Returns the anisotropic dimension of a symmetric bilinear form

- **Package:** [A1BrouwerDegrees](../../A1BrouwerDegrees/package/A1BrouwerDegrees.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/A1BrouwerDegrees/Code/Isotropy.m2:10:18-10:41`
- **Result type:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Aliases:** `A1BrouwerDegrees$getAnisotropicDimension`

## Description
By the Witt Decomposition Theorem, any non-degenerate form decomposes uniquely as $\beta \cong n \mathbb{H} \oplus \beta_a$ where the form $\beta_a$ is anisotropic. The rank of $\beta_a$ is called the anisotropic dimension of $\beta$.

The anisotropic dimension of a form defined over the rational numbers is the maximum of the [getAnisotropicDimensionQQp](../../A1BrouwerDegrees/methodFunction/getAnisotropicDimensionQQp.md) anisotropic dimension at each of the completions of $\mathbb{Q}$ at the [getRelevantPrimes](../../A1BrouwerDegrees/methodFunction/getRelevantPrimes.md).

### References

[KC18] P. Koprowski, A. Czogala, "Computing with quadratic forms over number fields," Journal of Symbolic Computation, 2018.

## Parameters
- **beta** — a "Grothendieck-Witt Class", a GrothendieckWittClass over a field $k$, where $k$ is $\mathbb{Q}$, $\mathbb{R}$, $\mathbb{C}$, or a finite field of characteristic not 2

## Returns
an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the rank of the anisotropic part of $\beta$

## Methods
- [`getAnisotropicDimension(Matrix)`](#getanisotropicdimensionmatrix)
- [`getAnisotropicDimension(GrothendieckWittClass)`](#getanisotropicdimensiongrothendieckwittclass)

## Source
