# getLocalA1Degree
Computes a local $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree of a list of $n$ polynomials in $n$ variables over a field $k$ at a prime ideal in the zero locus

- **Package:** [A1BrouwerDegrees](../../A1BrouwerDegrees/package/A1BrouwerDegrees.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/A1BrouwerDegrees/Code/LocalGlobalDegrees.m2:141:0-141:16`
- **Aliases:** `A1BrouwerDegrees$getLocalA1Degree`

## Description
Given an endomorphism of affine space $f=(f_{1},\ldots, f_{n}):\mathbb{A}^{n}_{k}\to\mathbb{A}^{n}_{k}$ and an isolated zero $p\in V(f)$, we may compute its local $\mathbb{A}^{1}$-Brouwer degree valued in the Grothendieck-Witt ring $\text{GW}(k)$.

For historical and mathematical background, see [getGlobalA1Degree](../../A1BrouwerDegrees/methodFunction/getGlobalA1Degree.md).

The sum of the local A1-degrees is equal to the global A1-degree:

## Parameters
- **L** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of polynomials $f=(f_{1}, \ldots, f_{n})$ in the polynomial ring $k[x_{1},\dots,x_{n}]$ where $k$ is $\mathbb{C}$, $\mathbb{Q}$, or a finite field of characteristic not 2. Over $\mathbb{R}$, the user is prompted to instead do the computation over $\mathbb{Q}$ and then base change to $\mathbb{R}$.
- **p** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a prime ideal $p\subset k[x_{1},\dots,x_{n}]$ corresponding to a point in the zero locus $V(f)$

## Returns
a "Grothendieck-Witt Class", the class $\text{deg}_{p}^{\mathbb{A}^{1}}(f)$ in the Grothendieck-Witt ring $\text{GW}(k)$

## Methods
- [`getLocalA1Degree(List,Ideal)`](#getlocala1degreelistideal)

## Examples
```macaulay2
T1 = QQ[z_1..z_2];
```

```macaulay2
f1 = {(z_1 - 1)*z_1*z_2, (3/5)*z_1^2 - (17/3)*z_2^2};
```

```macaulay2
q = ideal(z_1, z_2);
```

```
o3 : Ideal of T1
```

```macaulay2
r = ideal(z_1-1, z_2^2 - 9/85);
```

```
o4 : Ideal of T1
```

```macaulay2
f1LDq = getLocalA1Degree(f1, q)
```

```
o5 = | 0    0     0    17/3  |
     | 0    3/5   0    -17/3 |
     | 0    0     17/3 0     |
     | 17/3 -17/3 0    0     |
o5 : GrothendieckWittClass
```

```macaulay2
f1LDr = getLocalA1Degree(f1, r)
```

```
o6 = | -3/5 0     |
     | 0    -17/3 |
o6 : GrothendieckWittClass
```

```macaulay2
f1LDsum = addGW(f1LDq,f1LDr);
```

```macaulay2
f1GD = getGlobalA1Degree f1;
```

```macaulay2
isIsomorphicForm(f1GD,f1LDsum)
```

