# courantFunctions
Returns the Courant functions of a simplicial complex

- **Package:** [AlgebraicSplines](../../AlgebraicSplines/package/AlgebraicSplines.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/AlgebraicSplines.m2:570:0-570:16`
- **Result type:** [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md)
- **Aliases:** `AlgebraicSplines$courantFunctions`

## Description
This method returns a matrix with as many rows as facets and as many columns as vertices. Column $i$ of the matrix is the Courant function corresponding to vertex $V_i$. This is the piecewise linear function which takes the value $1$ at the vertex $V_i$ and $0$ at all other vertices.If the option Homogenize=>false is given, the Courant function corresponding to a cone vertex (if there is one) will be discarded.The Courant functions are used to construct the Stanley Reisner ring of a simplicial complex.

## Parameters
- **F** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of facets, recorded as indices of V
- **V** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of vertex coordinates

## Returns
M, a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a matrix so that column $i$ is the Courant function corresponding to vertex $V_i$

## Options
- **[InputType](../../FourTiTwo/symbol/InputType.md)** (default: `ByFacets`)
- **[Homogenize](../../Topcom/symbol/Homogenize.md)** (default: `true`)
- **[VariableName](../../Schubert2/symbol/VariableName.md)** (default: `t`)
- **[CoefficientRing](../../Core/symbol/CoefficientRing.md)** (default: `QQ`)
- **[BaseRing](../../AlgebraicSplines/symbol/BaseRing.md)**

## Methods
- [`courantFunctions(List,List)`](#courantfunctionslistlist)

## Examples
```macaulay2
V={{0,0},{0,1},{-1,-1},{1,0}};
```

```macaulay2
F={{0,1,2},{0,2,3},{0,1,3}};
```

```macaulay2
courantFunctions(V,F)
```

```
o3 = | 2t_0-t_1+t_2  -t_0+t_1 -t_0 0       |
     | -t_0+2t_1+t_2 0        -t_1 t_0-t_1 |
     | -t_0-t_1+t_2  t_1      0    t_0     |
                        3                 4
o3 : Matrix (QQ[t ..t ])  <-- (QQ[t ..t ])
                 0   2             0   2
```

```macaulay2
S=QQ[x,y];
```

```macaulay2
courantFunctions(V,F,Homogenize=>false,BaseRing=>S)
```

```
o5 = | -x+y -x 0   |
     | 0    -y x-y |
     | y    0  x   |
             3      3
o5 : Matrix S  <-- S
```

