# deRham
DeRham cohomology groups for the complement of a hypersurface

- **Package:** [BernsteinSato](../../BernsteinSato/package/BernsteinSato.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/BernsteinSato/DeRham.m2:12:0-12:6`
- **Aliases:** `BernsteinSato$deRham`

## Description
The algorithm used appears in the paper 'An algorithm for deRham cohomology groups of the complement of an affine variety via D-module computation' by Oaku-Takayama(1999). The method is to compute the localization of the polynomial ring by f, then compute the derived integration of the localization.

## Parameters
- **f** — a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md)
- **i** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)

## Returns
Mi, a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), the i-th deRham cohomology group of the complement of the hypersurface {f = 0}; M, a [HashTable](../../Core/type/HashTable.md), containing the entries of the form i=>Mi

## Options
- **[Strategy](../../Core/symbol/Strategy.md)** (default: `Schreyer`)

## Methods
- [`deRham(Ideal)`](#derhamideal)
- [`deRham(ZZ,Ideal)`](#derhamzzideal)
- [`deRham(RingElement)`](#derhamringelement)
- [`deRham(ZZ,RingElement)`](#derhamzzringelement)

