- **Aliases:** `Chordal$chordalNet`

## Description
This method constructs a chordal network from a given polynomial set F. This chordal network is a directed graph, whose nodes define a partition of F. The arcs of the directed graph are given by the [elimTree](../../Chordal/methodFunction/elimTree.md) of the associated [constraintGraph](../../Chordal/methodFunction/constraintGraph.md).

Selecting a good variable ordering is very important for the complexity of chordal networks methods. The variable ordering can be specified in the input. Alternatively, the string "SuggestOrder" can be used.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md),
- **str** — a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), (optional)
- **X** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of variables (optional)

