# reduceDimension
Removes arcs of a chordal network of small dimension

- **Package:** [Chordal](../../Chordal/package/Chordal.md)
- **Class:** [FunctionClosure](../../Core/type/FunctionClosure.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Chordal.m2:1620:18-1646:1`
- **Aliases:** `Chordal$reduceDimension`

## Description
Reduces a chordal network, by prunning the arcs that do not belong to the top $k$ dimensional parts of the variety.

The method [topComponents(ChordalNet)](topComponents_lpar_ChordalNet_rpar_.md) is equivalent to `reduceDimension(N,1)`.

#### Caveat
An arc is removed only if all the [ChordalNetChain](../../Chordal/type/ChordalNetChain.md) through it have small dimension. If an arc belongs to a chain of large dimension and a chain of small dimension, then the arc will not be removed.

#### Consequences
The input chordal network is modified

## Parameters
- **k** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md),
- **N** — an instance of the type "ChordalNet",

## Returns
no output,

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[a..j,MonomialOrder=>Lex];
```

```macaulay2
I = ideal {a*d - b*c, c*f - d*e, e*h - f*g, g*j - h*i, a*j - b*i};
```

```
o2 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
N = chordalNet I;
```

```macaulay2
chordalTria N;
```

```macaulay2
codimCount N
       7      6      5    4
```

```
o5 = 2t  + 17t  + 14t  + t
o5 : ZZ[t]
```

```macaulay2
reduceDimension(N,2);
```

```macaulay2
codimCount N
        5    4
```

```
o7 = 14t  + t
o7 : ZZ[t]
```

```macaulay2
reduceDimension(N,1);
```

```macaulay2
codimCount N
      4
```

```
o9 = t
o9 : ZZ[t]
```

## Source
```m2
reduceDimension = (N,k) -> (
    tree:= N.elimTree;
    (nodeTab,rankTab) := getCdimTable(N);
    nodeTab = applyPairs(nodeTab, (Nj,cdims)->(Nj,min(cdims)));
    nods := append(nodes(N), null);
    regret := new MutableHashTable from for Nj in nods list 
            if Nj===null then Nj=>0 else Nj=>infinity;
    for jp in nodePairs(tree,Reverse=>true) do (
        (j,p):= jp;
        nodesj := nodes(N,j);
        nodesp := if p===null then {null}
            else nodes(N,p);
        for Np in nodesp do (
            NJ:= if p=!=null then nodeChildren(j,Np) else nodesj;
            cdim := min(NJ / (Nj->nodeTab#Nj));
            for Nj in NJ do(
                regretjp := regret#Np + (nodeTab#Nj - cdim);
                if regretjp >= k then(
                    if Np=!=null then removeArc(Nj,Np);
                    if #Nj.parents==0 then deleteNode(N.net#j,Nj);
                );
                regret#Nj = min(regretjp,regret#Nj);
            );
        );
    );
    checkConsistency N;
)
```

