# exteriorHomologyModule
Make the homology of a complex into a module over an exterior algebra

- **Package:** [CompleteIntersectionResolutions](../../CompleteIntersectionResolutions/package/CompleteIntersectionResolutions.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/CompleteIntersectionResolutions.m2:1328:0-1328:22`
- **Result type:** [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md)
- **Aliases:** `CompleteIntersectionResolutions$exteriorHomologyModule`

## Description
Assuming that the elements of the 1xc matrix ff are null-homotopic on C, the script returns the direct sum of the homology of C as a module over a new ring, consisting of ring C with c exterior variables adjoined. The script is the main component of exteriorTorModule

## Parameters
- **C** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md),
- **ff** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), Matrix of elements that are homotopic to 0 on C

## Returns
M, a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md),

## Methods
