# closeIn
Close an input file

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [Manipulator](../../Core/type/Manipulator.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Aliases:** `Core$closeIn`

## Description
`f << closeIn` -- closes the input file `f`.`closeIn f` -- closes the input file `f`.

If the file was open only for input, then [close](../../Core/function/close.md) is easier to use and has the same effect.

If the file was open for both input and output, it remains open for output.

