## Description
There are two basic types of documentation:

Documenting a function or a method, as in [ideal(List)](ideal_lpar_List_rpar_.md).documenting an overview or functions with methods, as in [ideals](../../WeilDivisors/symbol/ideals.md) or [ideal](../../Core/methodFunction/ideal.md) respectively. The headings [Usage](../../Core/symbol/Usage.md), [BaseFunction](../../Core/symbol/BaseFunction.md), [Inputs](../../Core/symbol/Inputs.md), [Outputs](../../Core/symbol/Outputs.md), and [Consequences](../../Core/symbol/Consequences.md), are useful only for documentation of the first type, as well as in a call to [SYNOPSIS](../../Core/methodFunction/SYNOPSIS.md).

