# endPackage
End a new package

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/packages.m2:326:17-326:27`
- **Result type:** [Package](../../Core/type/Package.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$endPackage`

## Description
A package writer need not call this function explicitly, since the end of file hook for the file containing the [newPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/newPackage.md) command that opened the package will call [endPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/endPackage.md).

This function is called automatically at the end of a file, so package authors don't need to explicitly call `endPackage`.

#### Consequences
The package named should have been opened with [newPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/newPackage.md). The package is closed, and the former value of [dictionaryPath](../../Core/object/dictionaryPath.md) is restored, with the global dictionary (containing the exported symbols) of the package prepended.

## Parameters
- **pkgname** — a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), the name of the package

## Returns
a [Package](../../Core/type/Package.md), the new package

## Methods
- [`endPackage(String)`](#endpackagestring)

## Examples
```macaulay2
newPackage "Foo"
```

