# endl
End an output line

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [Manipulator](../../Core/type/Manipulator.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Aliases:** `Core$endl`

## Description
`f << endl` -- ends the line currently being put out to the file `f`.

It is an essential portable programming practice to use `endl` always, for writing newline characters (see [newline](../../Core/object/newline.md)) to a file will not terminate a line containing nets properly, and it will not flush the output buffer.

