# installPackage
Load and install a package and its documentation

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/installPackage.m2:326:33-326:47`
- **Result type:** [Package](../../Core/type/Package.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$installPackage`

## Description
The main action of this routine is to generate the documentation of the given package and install the Macaulay2 package and documentation.

The actual file loaded is `PackageName.m2`, which should be on the load [path](../../Core/object/path.md) and should contain a package named `PackageName`.

In order to accomplish this, several steps are performed (or bypassed, depending on the values of the optional arguments).

load the package, if not already loaded (see [loadPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/loadPackage.md))determine which help pages have changed since last installrun any new or previously failed examples, or all examples, as specified by the `RerunExamples` optiongenerate the html pages, or not, as specified by the `MakeHTML` option, for the modified help pages, or all html pages if `RemakeAllDocumentation` is set to truegenerate the info pages, or not, as specified by the `MakeInfo` optioninstall the documentation and package in the location specified by the `InstallPrefix` optionplace a link to this html documentation in the file `index.html` in the user's [application directory](application_spc_directory.md); see [makePackageIndex](../../Core/methodFunction/makePackageIndex.md)The current value of [prefixPath](../../Core/object/prefixPath.md) is used to determine how to direct documentation hyperlinks; the link will be directed to the appropriate file if one is found by searching the trees referred to by [prefixPath](../../Core/object/prefixPath.md). Otherwise, all documentation hyperlinks are relative to positions within a single tree of directories, as describe by [Layout](../../Core/table/Layout.md).

It might be necessary to run [installPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/installPackage.md) twice if a package with the same name is already installed: the second installation will redirect the hyperlinks to the freshly installed documentation, because the files will have been installed by the first installation. This applies, for example, to those authors who are developing updates to packages already included with Macaulay2.

The files of the package are placed in subdirectories of the appropriate prefix directory as specified by [Layout](../../Core/table/Layout.md), depending on the value of the `SeparateExec` option:

Install paths given `SeparateExec => false`:`share/Macaulay2/PackageName.m2`,`share/info/PackageName.info`,`lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/`,`share/Macaulay2/PackageName/`, and`share/doc/Macaulay2/PackageName/`; Install paths given `SeparateExec => true`:`common/share/Macaulay2/PackageName.m2`,`common/share/info/PackageName.info`,`x86_64-Linux-ArchLinux/lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/`,`common/share/Macaulay2/PackageName/`, and`common/share/doc/Macaulay2/PackageName/`. Note that in the latter case, the paths reflect the type of your machine. In addition, if no errors occurred during running the examples, then an empty file whose name is `lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/.installed` or `x86_64-Linux-ArchLinux/lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/.installed` is created, to signify that installation was completed.

#### Caveat
Links from html files containing documentation to documentation in another package not yet installed may go to the wrong place, because it is assumed that the package not yet installed will be installed under the same prefix. By contrast, if the other package has already been installed under some prefix occurring in the value of [prefixPath](../../Core/object/prefixPath.md), then the correct path will be used.  To get two packages installed under different prefixes which refer to each other's documentation correctly, it may be necessary to install one of them twice.

#### Consequences
The package is installed in a local directory, so that in the future, one may simply use [loadPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/loadPackage.md). Documentation for the package is also produced, running any Macaulay2 examples that are requested in the package documentation, with the random number seed initialized to 0.

## Parameters
- **PackageName** — a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), or "Package", the package to install

## Returns
a [Package](../../Core/type/Package.md), the package that was installed

