# isWellDefined
Whether a map is well defined

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/methods.m2:363:15-363:28`
- **Result type:** [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$isWellDefined`

## Description
In order to check whether a matrix, whose source module is not free, is well defined, then a Gröbner basis computation will probably be required. In order to check whether a ring map is well defined, it is often necessary to check that the image of an ideal under a related ring map is zero.  This often requires a Gröbner basis as well.

## Parameters
- **f** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md) or a [RingMap](../../Core/type/RingMap.md)

## Returns
a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md), whether f is a well-defined map

