# makePackageIndex
Create an index of installed packages

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionSingle](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionSingle.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/installPackage.m2:319:0-319:16`
- **Aliases:** `Core$makePackageIndex`

## Description
This command may need to be run after installing a package via [installPackage](../../Core/methodFunction/installPackage.md).

This command is run each time the program is started, updating the index file. Thus, one can simply restart Macaulay2 to obtain the same consequence.

#### Consequences
Creates a file `index.html` in the `~/. Macaulay2` directory, containing links to the documentation for Macaulay2 and all installed packages.

## Methods
- [`makePackageIndex(Sequence)`](#makepackageindexsequence)
- [`makePackageIndex(List)`](#makepackageindexlist)

## Source
