# newRing
Make a copy of a ring, with some features changed

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/newring.m2:16:0-16:7`
- **Result type:** [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$newRing`

## Description
If a different number of variables is given with [Variables](../../Core/symbol/Variables.md), then the list of degrees in `R` will be ignored.  If a new degree rank is specified with [DegreeRank](../../Core/symbol/DegreeRank.md) then the list of degrees and the heft vector of `R` will be ignored.  If a new nonempty list of degrees is specified with [Degrees](../../Core/symbol/Degrees.md), then the degree rank and the heft vector of `R` will be ignored.

The default values for the options of `newRing` are all set to a non-accessible private symbol whose name is `nothing`.

## Parameters
- **R** — a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md) or a [QuotientRing](../../Core/type/QuotientRing.md),

## Returns
S, a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), a new ring, constructed in the same way R was, over the same coefficient ring, but with the newly specified options overriding those used before. See [Monoid](../../Core/type/Monoid.md) for a description of those options. If R was a quotient ring, then the number of variables must be the same, and S will be a quotient ring, too, with defining ideal obtained from the old by substituting the new variables for the old, preserving their order.

## Methods
- [`newRing(PolynomialRing)`](#newringpolynomialring)
- [`newRing(QuotientRing)`](#newringquotientring)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y, MonomialOrder => Lex, Degrees => {3,5}];
```

```macaulay2
describe newRing(R, MonomialOrder => GRevLex)
```

```
o2 = QQ[x..y, Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32}]
                                                               {GRevLex => {3, 5} }
                                                               {Position => Up    }
```

```macaulay2
describe newRing(R, Variables => 4)
```

```
o3 = QQ[p ..p , Degrees => {4:1}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32}]
         0   3                                                  {Lex => 2          }
                                                                {Position => Up    }
                                                                {GRevLex => {2:1}  }
```

```macaulay2
describe newRing(R, Heft => {2})
```

```
o4 = QQ[x..y, Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {2}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32}]
                                                               {Lex => 2          }
                                                               {Position => Up    }
```

```macaulay2
S = R/(x^2+y^3);
```

```macaulay2
describe newRing(R, Variables => 2)
```

```
o6 = QQ[p ..p , Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32}]
         0   1                                                   {Lex => 2          }
                                                                 {Position => Up    }
```

