Symmetric power

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/m2/matrix1.m2:486:38-486:52`
- **Aliases:** `Core$symmetricPower`

## Description
There is currently one restriction: if $f$ is a matrix, then it must have only one row, and be a map of free modules, as in this example.

If G --> F --> M --> 0 is a presentation for the module M = coker(f: G-->F), then symmetricPower(i, f) is the cokernel of the map symmetricPower(i-1, F) ** G --> symmetricPower(i, F).

## Parameters
- **i** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md),
- **M** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), or a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md)

## Returns
a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), or a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), the $i$-th symmetric power of the matrix or module $f$

