# findIdempotents
Construct idempotent endomorphisms

- **Package:** [DirectSummands](../../DirectSummands/package/DirectSummands.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/DirectSummands/idempotents.m2:100:0-100:15`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `DirectSummands$findIdem`, `DirectSummands$findIdempotents`, `findIdem`

## Description
This routine constructs nontrivial idempotents in the endomorphism algebra of a module. When successful, those idempotents can be used to recover direct sum decompositions. This is the main splitting strategy for modules over local rings.

## Parameters
- **M** — a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md) or a [CoherentSheaf](../../Varieties/type/CoherentSheaf.md),

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of idempotent endomorphisms of $M$ suitable for splitting

## Methods
- [`findIdempotents(CoherentSheaf)`](#findidempotentscoherentsheaf)
- [`findIdempotents(Module)`](#findidempotentsmodule)

## Source
