# homotopyEDDegree
Numerically compute ED degrees of affine cones using homotopy continuation

- **Package:** [EuclideanDistanceDegree](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/package/EuclideanDistanceDegree.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/EuclideanDistanceDegree/Numerical.m2:96:0-96:16`
- **Result type:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Aliases:** `EuclideanDistanceDegree$homotopyEDDegree`

## Description
Executes the homotopy defined by the passed in [NumericalComputationOptions](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/type/NumericalComputationOptions.md) object. A weight homotopy will vary the weights of the distance function whereas a data homotopy will vary the data point. A stage1 homotopy solves the start system as defined in NCO whereas stage2 will perform the weight/data homotopy to solve the defined target system. It is possible to perform stage2 multiple times for different target systems without rerunning stage1, but at least one stage1 homotopy must be executed in the directory specified in NCO for stage2 to executed properly.

#### Caveat
Inaccurate results may be returned if $V(F)$ is contained in $V(L)$. The computed ED degree may be lower than expected due to path tracking.

## Parameters
- **ht** — a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), one of "Weight" or "Data" which defines the type of homotopy to execute
- **isStageOne** — a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md), if set, runs stage 1 to solve the start system
- **isStageTwo** — a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md), if set, runs stage 2 to solve the target system via path tracking
- **NCO** — an instance of the type "NumericalComputationOptions", a MutableHashTable to keeps track of the options and configurations for the homotopy methods

## Returns
ED, an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), a generic/unit Euclidean distance degree

## Methods
- [`homotopyEDDegree(NumericalComputationOptions,String,Boolean,Boolean)`](#homotopyeddegreenumericalcomputationoptionsstringbooleanboolean)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y];
```

```macaulay2
F = G = {x^2+y^2-1};
```

```macaulay2
NCO = newNumericalComputationOptions(F, G);
```

```macaulay2
NCO#"TargetWeight" = apply(#gens R, i -> random RR);
```

```macaulay2
GED = homotopyEDDegree(NCO, "Weight", true, true)
-- warning: experimental computation over inexact field begun
--          results not reliable (one warning given per session)
```

```
o5 = 4
```

```macaulay2
NCO#"TargetWeight" = apply(#gens R, i -> 1_R);
```

```macaulay2
UED = homotopyEDDegree(NCO, "Weight", false, true)
```

```
o7 = 2
```

## Source
