# newNumericalComputationOptions
Define homotopy options and configurations

- **Package:** [EuclideanDistanceDegree](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/package/EuclideanDistanceDegree.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/EuclideanDistanceDegree/Numerical.m2:28:0-28:30`
- **Aliases:** `EuclideanDistanceDegree$newNumericalComputationOptions`

## Description
Creates a [NumericalComputationOptions](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/type/NumericalComputationOptions.md) object. At mimumum it requires the model $F$ for which the ED Degree will be computed and a witness model $G$. A submodel $L$ may be passed in to "slice" the variety, by default it will be the empty set. A String indicating the temporary directory from which Bertini will read/write files during the run may also be passed in as an optional argument, by default it will be a random temporary file name. The temporary directory will be created if it does not exist.

## Parameters
- **F** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a system of polynomials (need not be square) defining the variety
- **G** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a system of polynomials (complete intersection) such that V(F) is an irreducible component of V(G), i.e. a witness model

## Returns
NCO, an instance of the type "NumericalComputationOptions", a MutableHashTable to keep track of options and configurations for the homotopy methods

## Options
- **[TempDirectory](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/symbol/TempDirectory.md)**
- **[Submodel](../../EuclideanDistanceDegree/symbol/Submodel.md)** (default: `{}`)

## Methods
- [`newNumericalComputationOptions(List,List)`](#newnumericalcomputationoptionslistlist)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y];
```

```macaulay2
F = G = {x^2 + y^2 - 1};
```

```macaulay2
dir = temporaryFileName();
```

```macaulay2
NCO = newNumericalComputationOptions(F, G, TempDirectory => dir);
```

```macaulay2
NCO#"TargetWeight" = apply(#gens R, i -> 1_R);
```

```macaulay2
UED = homotopyEDDegree(NCO, "Weight", true, true)
-- warning: experimental computation over inexact field begun
--          results not reliable (one warning given per session)
```

```
o6 = 2
```

