# lieAlgebra
Make a free Lie algebra

- **Package:** [GradedLieAlgebras](../../GradedLieAlgebras/package/GradedLieAlgebras.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/GradedLieAlgebras.m2:188:25-188:35`
- **Result type:** [LieAlgebra](../../LieAlgebraRepresentations/type/LieAlgebra.md)
- **Aliases:** `GradedLieAlgebras$lieAlgebra`

## Description
A generator may be of class `Symbol` or `IndexedVariable`. The same name for a generator can be used in several Lie algebras and also as name for a variable in a polynomial ring. If a symbol $a$ has been used as name for some output, then you must write `a = symbol a` to be able to use the symbol as a generator instead. Relations are introduced by the operator /, see [LieAlgebra / List](LieAlgebra_spc__slash__spc_List.md). It is also possible to define a Lie algebra modulo an ideal. A differential Lie algebra is defined by giving the value of the differential on the generators, see [differentialLieAlgebra](../../GradedLieAlgebras/methodFunction/differentialLieAlgebra.md). If relations are introduced as a list, then the program adds relations to make the ideal of relations invariant under the differential. These non-normalized relations are obtained using [ideal(LieAlgebra)](ideal_lpar_LieAlgebra_rpar_.md) and can also be seen using [describe(LieAlgebra)](describe_lpar_LieAlgebra_rpar_.md), see `L2` below. The zero Lie algebra (over `QQ`) is defined as `lieAlgebra\{\}`.

## Parameters
- **liegens** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of elements of class Symbol or IndexedVariable

## Returns
L, an instance of the type "LieAlgebra",

## Options
- **[Weights](../../Core/symbol/Weights.md)** — optional argument for lieAlgebra (default: `1`)
- **[Signs](../../GradedLieAlgebras/symbol/Signs.md)** — optional argument for lieAlgebra (default: `0`)
- **[Field](../../PolyominoIdeals/symbol/Field.md)** — optional argument for lieAlgebra (default: `QQ`)
- **[LastWeightHomological](../../GradedLieAlgebras/symbol/LastWeightHomological.md)** — optional argument for lieAlgebra (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`lieAlgebra(List)`](#liealgebralist)

## Examples
