# gaussianVanishingIdeal
Vanishing ideal of a Gaussian graphical model

- **Package:** [GraphicalModels](../../GraphicalModels/package/GraphicalModels.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/GraphicalModels.m2:969:0-969:22`
- **Result type:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md)
- **Aliases:** `GraphicalModels$gaussianVanishingIdeal`

## Description
`gaussianVanishingIdeal` computes the ideal in $R$ of homogeneous polynomial relations on the variance-covariance parameters of a graphical model on $G$ as explained in Chapter 3.3 of ``Lectures on Algebraic Statistics'' by Drton, Sturmfels, and Sullivant.

This method works for graphs, digraphs and mixed graphs without undirected edges.

#### Caveat
This method currently works on really small examples because it computes the vanishing ideal as an elimination ideal.

## Parameters
- **R** — a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), created with "gaussianRing" using a graphs of classes "Graph", "Digraph" or "MixedGraph" without undirected edges as input.

## Returns
an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), ideal in R

## Options
- **[OldVersion](../../GraphicalModels/symbol/OldVersion.md)** — optional argument in gaussianVanishingIdeal to use old method for gaussianRings coming from directed graphs (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`gaussianVanishingIdeal(Ring)`](#gaussianvanishingidealring)

## Examples
```macaulay2
G = graph({{a,b},{b,c},{c,d},{a,d}})
```

```
o1 = Graph{a => {b, d}}
           b => {a, c}
           c => {b, d}
           d => {a, c}
o1 : Graph
```

```macaulay2
R = gaussianRing G
```

```
o2 = R
o2 : PolynomialRing
```

```macaulay2
J = gaussianVanishingIdeal(R);
```

```
o3 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
ideal mingens J / print;
                    2
s   s   s    - s   s    - s   s   s    + s   s   s    + s   s   s    - s   s   s
 a,d b,c b,d    a,c b,d    a,d b,b c,d    a,b b,d c,d    a,c b,b d,d    a,b b,c d,d
                2
s   s   s    - s   s    - s   s   s    + s   s   s    + s   s   s    - s   s   s
 a,c a,d b,c    a,c b,d    a,b a,d c,c    a,a b,d c,c    a,b a,c c,d    a,a b,c c,d
```

```macaulay2
G = digraph {{a,{b,c}}, {b,{c,d}}, {c,{}}, {d,{}}}
```

```
o5 = Digraph{a => {c, b}}
             b => {c, d}
             c => {}
             d => {}
o5 : Digraph
```

```macaulay2
R = gaussianRing G
```

```
o6 = R
o6 : PolynomialRing
```

```macaulay2
gaussianVanishingIdeal(R)
```

```
o7 = ideal (s   s    - s   s   , s   s    - s   s   , s   s    - s   s   )
             b,c b,d    b,b c,d   a,d b,c    a,b c,d   a,d b,b    a,b b,d
o7 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
H = mixedGraph(digraph {{a,{c}},{b,{c}}, {c,{d}}},bigraph {{c,d}})
```

```
o8 = MixedGraph{Bigraph => Bigraph{c => {d}}}
                                   d => {c}
                Digraph => Digraph{a => {c}}
                                   b => {c}
                                   c => {d}
                                   d => {}
                Graph => Graph{}
o8 : MixedGraph
```

```macaulay2
S = gaussianRing H
```

```
o9 = S
o9 : PolynomialRing
```

```macaulay2
gaussianVanishingIdeal(S)
```

```
o10 = ideal (s   , s   s    - s   s   )
              a,b   a,d b,c    a,c b,d
o10 : Ideal of S
```

