# addEdges'
A method for adding edges to a graph

- **Package:** [Graphs](../../Graphs/package/Graphs.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Graphs.m2:546:40-546:49`
- **Aliases:** `Graphs$addEdges'`

## Description
This method will take in a Graph and a List of new edges, and output a graph with these new edges along with the previous edges.

## Parameters
- **G** — a "graph",
- **L** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), This List should be composed of other Lists, just as one would input an edge set
- **S** — a [Set](../../Core/type/Set.md), This is used when only one edge needs to be used via addEdge

## Returns
