# digraph
Constructs a digraph

- **Package:** [Graphs](../../Graphs/package/Graphs.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Graphs.m2:252:0-252:7`
- **Aliases:** `Graphs$digraph`

## Description
A digraph is a set of vertices connected by directed edges. Unlike the case with simple graphs, {u, v} being an edge does not imply that {v, u} is also an edge. Notably, this allows for non-symmetric adjacency matrices.

## Parameters
- **A** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), Denotes an adjacency matrix
- **E** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), Denotes an edge list (a list of ordered pair lists)
- **H** — a [HashTable](../../Core/type/HashTable.md),
- **V** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), Denotes a vertex list

## Returns
G, a "digraph",

## Options
- **[Singletons](../../Graphs/symbol/Singletons.md)**
- **[EntryMode](../../Graphs/symbol/EntryMode.md)** (default: `auto`)

