# girth
A method for computing the girth of a graph

- **Package:** [Graphs](../../Graphs/package/Graphs.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Graphs.m2:1015:0-1015:5`
- **Result type:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Aliases:** `Graphs$girth`

## Description
This method computes the girth (the smallest n such that G contains an n-cycle) of any graph. If the graph has no n-cycle as a subgraph, the output will be infinity.

## Parameters
- **G** — a "graph",

## Returns
g, an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the girth of G

## Methods
- [`girth(Graph)`](#girthgraph)

## Examples
```macaulay2
girth completeGraph 6
```

```
o1 = 3
```

```macaulay2
girth pathGraph 6
```

```
o2 = infinity
o2 : InfiniteNumber
```

## Source
