```

## Method details
### `girth(Graph)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Graphs.m2:1016:24-1043:5`
- **Domain:** [Graph](../../MonodromySolver/symbol/Graph.md)
- **Returns:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md) (common typical value)

#### Source
```m2
girth Graph := Thing => G -> (
    g := infinity;
    n := #vertexSet G;
    P := new MutableList from toList(n:0);
    D := new MutableList from toList(n:0);
    for v from 0 to n-1 do (
        S := {};
        R := {v};
        P#v = null;
        D#v = 0;
        while R != {} do(
            x := first R;
            S = append(S, x);
            R = drop(R, 1);
            L := positions(first entries (adjacencyMatrix G)^{x}, j -> j != 0) - set {P#x};
            for y in L do (
                if member(y, S) then
                    ( g = min {g, D#y + D#x + 1}; )
                else(
                    P#y = x;
                    D#y = 1 + D#x;
                    R = unique append(R, y);
                    );
                );
            );
        );
    g
    )
```

