# hasEulerianTrail
Determines whether a graph or a digraph has an Eulerian trail

- **Package:** [Graphs](../../Graphs/package/Graphs.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Graphs.m2:1225:0-1225:16`
- **Result type:** [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md)
- **Aliases:** `Graphs$hasEulerianTrail`

## Description
A graph has an Eulerian trail if there is a path in the graph that visits each edge exactly once.  A digraph has a Eulerian trail if there is a directed path in the graph that visits each edge exactly once.  An Eulerian trail is also called an Eulerian path.  Unconnected graphs can have a Eulerian trail, but all vertices of degree greater than 0 of a graph (or all vertices of degree greater than 0 in the underlying graph of a digraph) must belong to a single connected component.

## Parameters
- **D** — a "digraph",
- **G** — a "graph",

## Returns
E, a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md), whether G or D has an Eulerian trail

## Methods
- [`hasEulerianTrail(Graph)`](#haseuleriantrailgraph)
- [`hasEulerianTrail(Digraph)`](#haseuleriantraildigraph)

## Examples
```macaulay2
G = cycleGraph 5;
```

```macaulay2
hasEulerianTrail G
```

```
o2 = true
```

```macaulay2
D = digraph(toList(1..4), {{1,2},{2,3},{3,4}});
```

```macaulay2
hasEulerianTrail D
```

```
o4 = true
```

