# invSyzygies
Compute involutive basis of syzygies

- **Package:** [InvolutiveBases](../../InvolutiveBases/package/InvolutiveBases.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/InvolutiveBases.m2:525:0-525:11`
- **Result type:** [InvolutiveBasis](../../InvolutiveBases/type/InvolutiveBasis.md)
- **Aliases:** `InvolutiveBases$invSyzygies`

## Description
#### Caveat
cannot be iterated because [schreyerOrder](../../Core/methodFunction/schreyerOrder.md) is not used; call [janetResolution](../../InvolutiveBases/methodFunction/janetResolution.md) instead

## Parameters
- **J** — an instance of the type "InvolutiveBasis"

## Returns
an instance of the type "InvolutiveBasis", an involutive basis for the syzygies of J

## Methods
- [`invSyzygies(InvolutiveBasis)`](#invsyzygiesinvolutivebasis)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y,z];
```

```macaulay2
I = ideal(x,y,z);
```

```
o2 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
J = janetBasis I
     +-+---------+
```

```
o3 = |z|{z}      |
     +-+---------+
     |y|{z, y}   |
     +-+---------+
     |x|{z, y, x}|
     +-+---------+
o3 : InvolutiveBasis
```

```macaulay2
invSyzygies J
     +------+---------+
```

```
o4 = ||  x ||{z, y, x}|
     ||  0 ||         |
     || -z ||         |
     +------+---------+
     ||  y ||{z, y}   |
     || -z ||         |
     ||  0 ||         |
     +------+---------+
     ||  0 ||{z, y, x}|
     ||  x ||         |
     || -y ||         |
     +------+---------+
o4 : InvolutiveBasis
```

## Source
