# decomposeGradedModule
Decompose a graded module over a ring of graded module maps

- **Package:** [Kronecker](../../Kronecker/package/Kronecker.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Kronecker.m2:974:0-974:21`
- **Result type:** [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md)
- **Aliases:** `Kronecker$decomposeGradedModule`

## Description
Given maps `x` and `y` of degree 1 from a graded module `M` over a field k to `M`, we can think of `M` as a module over `k[x, y]`.  If `x^2=0`, `y^2=0`, and `x*y+y*x=0`, we can decompose `M` into a direct sum of simple modules.

## Parameters
- **x** — a [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md), a graded module map of degree 1
- **y** — a [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md), a graded module map of degree 1

## Returns
x', a [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md); y', a [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md); f, a [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md), an isomorphism

## Methods
- [`decomposeGradedModule(ComplexMap,ComplexMap)`](#decomposegradedmodulecomplexmapcomplexmap)

## Source
```m2
decomposeGradedModule = method()
```

## Method details
### `decomposeGradedModule(ComplexMap,ComplexMap)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Kronecker.m2:975:59-1058:6`
- **Domain:** [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md), [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md)
- **Returns:** [ComplexMap](../../Complexes/type/ComplexMap.md) (common typical value)

#### Source
```m2
decomposeGradedModule(GradedModuleMap, GradedModuleMap) := (x,y) -> (
     scan({x,y}, z -> (
	       if source z != target z then (
	       	    error "expected a map from a graded module to itself";
	       	    );
	       if degree z != 1 then (
		    error "expected a graded module map of degree 1";
		    );
	       if z*z != 0 then (
		    error "expected a graded module map which squares to zero";
		    );
	       ));
     if source x != source y then (
	  error "expected two maps on the same graded module";
	  );
     if x*y+y*x != 0 then (
	  error "expected graded module maps which anticommute";
	  );

     M := source x;
     Q := ring M;
     degList := toList(min M .. max M);

     p := x*y;
     mygens := flatten apply(degList, i -> apply(columns mingens image p_i, v -> (
		    src := new GradedModule;
		    src.ring = M.ring;
		    v1 := map(target p_i, , v) // p_i;
		    v2 := (x_i*v1) | (y_i*v1);
		    v3 := p_i*v1;
		    src#i = source v1;
		    src#(i+1) = source v2;
		    src#(i+2) = source v3;
		    injection map(M, src, j -> (
			      if j == i then (
				   map(M_j, , v1)
				   )
			      else if j == i+1 then (
				   map(M_j, , v2)
				   )
			      else if j == i+2 then (
				   map(M_j, , v3)
				   )
			      else 0
			      )
			 )
		    )));

     MM := ker p;
     mygens = mygens | flatten apply(degList, i -> (
	       tmpSrc := MM_i / image(x_(i-1) | y_(i-1));
	       if tmpSrc == 0 then {} else (
		    src := trim image map(MM_i, , id_tmpSrc // inducedMap(tmpSrc, MM_i));
	       	    inc := inducedMap(M_i, MM_i)*inducedMap(MM_i, src);
		    im := inducedMap(M_(i+1), MM_(i+1))*map(MM_(i+1), , 
			 mingens(image(x_i*inc) + image(y_i*inc)) // generators MM_(i+1));
	       	    (A,B,P1,P2) := kroneckerNormalForm((x_i*inc) // im, (y_i*inc) // im);
	       	    apply(#(components A), j -> (
			      v := map(M_i, , inc*P2*map(source P2, , (source A)_[j]));
			      w := map(M_(i+1), , im*P1^(-1)*map(target P1, , (target A)_[j]));
			      tmpGM := (gradedModule source v)[-i];
			      tmpGM#(i+1) = source w;
			      injection map(M, tmpGM, k -> (
				   	if k == i then map(M_k, tmpGM_k, v)
				   	else if k == i+1 then map(M_k, tmpGM_k, w)
				   	else map(M_k, tmpGM_k, 0)
				   	)
			      	   )
			      )
		    	 )
	       	    )
	       )
	  );

     (newx, newy) := apply((x,y), z -> directSum(apply(mygens, g -> (
			 map(source g, source g, j -> (
				   (z_j*g_j) // g_(j+1)
				   ), Degree => 1)
			 )
		    )
	       )
	  );
     (newx, newy, joinColumns(M, mygens))
     )
