# kustinMillerComplex
Compute Kustin-Miller resolution of the unprojection of I in J

- **Package:** [KustinMiller](../../KustinMiller/package/KustinMiller.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/KustinMiller.m2:307:0-307:19`
- **Result type:** [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md)
- **Aliases:** `KustinMiller$kustinMillerComplex`

## Description
Compute Kustin-Miller resolution of the unprojection of I in J (or equivalently of the image J' of J in R/I) with unprojection variable T.

We have the following setup:

Assume R is a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md) over a field, the degrees of all variables positive and $I \subset J \subset R$ two homogeneous ideals of R such that R/I and R/J are Gorenstein and dim(R/J)=dim(R/I)-1.

Let R/I(k_1) and R/J(k_2) be the canonical modules of R/I and R/J respectively. We require k_1 - k_2, that is, the degree of the unprojection variable, to be positive.

For a description of this resolution and how it is computed see

J. Boehm, S. Papadakis: Implementing the Kustin-Miller complex construction, [http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.2314](http://arxiv.org/abs/1103.2314)

It is also possible to specify minimal resolutions of I and J.

The function [kustinMillerComplex](../../KustinMiller/methodFunction/kustinMillerComplex.md) returns a chain complex over a new polynomial ring S with the same [coefficientRing](../../Core/methodFunction/coefficientRing.md) as R and the variables of R and W, where degree(T) = [degree](../../Core/methodFunction/degree.md) [unprojectionHomomorphism](../../KustinMiller/methodFunction/unprojectionHomomorphism.md)(I, J) = k_1-k_2.

To avoid printing the variables of this ring when printing the chain complex just give a name to the ring (e.g., do S = [ring](../../Core/methodFunction/ring.md) cc  to call it S).

We illustrate the Kustin-Miller complex construction at the example described in Section 5.5 of

Papadakis, Kustin-Miller unprojection with complexes,  J. Algebraic Geometry 13 (2004) 249-268, [http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0111195](http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0111195)

## Parameters
- **cI** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), resolution of I
- **cJ** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), resolution of J
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), contained in J
- **J** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), in a positively graded polynomial ring R
- **W** — a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md), over the same "coefficientRing" as R with one variable T.

## Returns
a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md),

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** — Option to print intermediate data (default: `0`)

## Methods
- [`kustinMillerComplex(Ideal,Ideal,PolynomialRing)`](#kustinmillercomplexidealidealpolynomialring)
- [`kustinMillerComplex(Complex,Complex,PolynomialRing)`](#kustinmillercomplexcomplexcomplexpolynomialring)

