# VInSymdW
Computes a basis of a submodule of $\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ isomorphic to $V$ with a given highest weight vector

- **Package:** [LieAlgebraRepresentations](../../LieAlgebraRepresentations/package/LieAlgebraRepresentations.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/LieAlgebraRepresentations/highestWeightVectorsAndSubmodules.m2:298:0-298:8`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `LieAlgebraRepresentations$VInSymdW`

## Description
Suppose that an irreducible module $V$ appears in the decomposition of $\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ with multiplicity at least one. Then we can find a highest weight vector using [weightMuHighestWeightVectorsInSymdW](../../LieAlgebraRepresentations/methodFunction/weightMuHighestWeightVectorsInSymdW.md), and then compute a basis of a submodule in $\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ isomorphic to $V$. The basis elements are expressed as polynomials in the basis of $W$ used to define the matrix generators of the representation on $W$.

We compute the degree four invariant for plane cubics by finding a trivial submodule in $\operatorname{Sym}^4 \operatorname{Sym}^3 \mathbb{C}^3$.

This polynomial appears as early as 1856 in work of Cayley, who attributes it to Salmon. See Cayley, "A third memoir upon quantics", tables 62 and 63.

## Parameters
- **d** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md),
- **hwv** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md),
- **V** — an instance of the type "LieAlgebraRepresentation",
- **W** — an instance of the type "LieAlgebraRepresentation",

## Returns
L, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Options
- **[SaveAsFunction](SaveAsFunction.md)**

## Methods
- [`VInSymdW(LieAlgebraRepresentation,ZZ,LieAlgebraRepresentation,Matrix)`](#vinsymdwliealgebrarepresentationzzliealgebrarepresentationmatrix)
- [`VInSymdW(LieAlgebraRepresentation,ZZ,LieAlgebraRepresentation,RingElement)`](#vinsymdwliealgebrarepresentationzzliealgebrarepresentationringelement)

## Examples
