# deGraafBases
Compute the bases produced by de Graaf's algorithm

- **Package:** [LieAlgebraRepresentations](../../LieAlgebraRepresentations/package/LieAlgebraRepresentations.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/LieAlgebraRepresentations/deGraafAlgorithm.m2:131:0-131:12`
- **Result type:** [Sequence](../../Core/type/Sequence.md)
- **Aliases:** `LieAlgebraRepresentations$deGraafBases`

## Description
This function implements the main algorithm in de Graaf, "Constructing representations of split semisimple Lie Algebras", J. Pure Appl. Algebra 164 (2001), no. 1-2, 87-107.

Let $V$ be an irreducible $\mathfrak{g}$-module with highest weight $\lambda$. Then $V$ may be constructed as the quotient of the algebra $U(N^{-})$ (see [uNminus](../../LieAlgebraRepresentations/methodFunction/uNminus.md)) by a left ideal $I$. de Graaf's algorithm produces a Gröbner basis of the ideal $I$, and a basis of the quotient $U(N^{-})/I$.

Note that de Graaf scales his basis monomials.  We skip this.

## Parameters
- **g** — an instance of the type "LieAlgebra",
- **lambda** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Returns
S, a [Sequence](../../Core/type/Sequence.md),

## Methods
