# macaulayOrders
Finds all orders with respect to which the poset is Macaulay

- **Package:** [MacaulayPosets](../../MacaulayPosets/package/MacaulayPosets.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/MacaulayPosets.m2:580:0-580:14`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `MacaulayPosets$macaulayOrders`

## Description
Given a poset with rank function $r$, this method returns all Macaulay orders [<list](<list.md). It is the permutation of the of the ground set of $P$ that is increasing with respect to [<TikZ](<TikZ.md) can print a Hasse diagram of the poset for each order [<QuotientRing](<QuotientRing.md) or an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), this method will not verify level linear independence.

