# schubertDecompose
Finds the decomposition of an ASM ideal into Schubert determinantal ideals

- **Package:** [MatrixSchubert](../../MatrixSchubert/package/MatrixSchubert.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/MatrixSchubert/MatrixSchubertConstructions.m2:555:0-555:17`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `MatrixSchubert$schubDecompose`, `MatrixSchubert$schubertDecompose`, `schubDecompose`

## Description
Given an ASM ideal $I_A$, it can be decomposed into Schubert determinantal ideals as $I_A = I_{w_1} \cap ... \cap I_{w_k}$, where the $w_i$ are permutations. As output, each element in the list is the permutation associated to a prime component in the Schubert decomposition of the antidiagonal initial ideal of $I$.

If the ASM ideal for an ASM $A$ has not het been computed, one may also give the ASM $A$ as input.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), or A is a "Matrix"

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

