# getCycles
Find cycles of graph

- **Package:** [Matroids](../../Matroids/package/Matroids.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Matroids.m2:165:13-165:22`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `Matroids$getCycles`

## Description
A cycle of G is a connected, 2-regular subgraph of G (i.e. every vertex has degree 2). This method returns all cycles of length at least 3, as ordered lists of vertices (for cycles of length 1 or 2, see the options Loops and ParallelEdges at [matroid](../../Matroids/methodFunction/matroid.md)). This method is used to create the graphic matroid: the output is in bijection with the circuits of the graphic matroid (excluding loops and parallel edges).

## Parameters
- **G** — a "graph",

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of (simple) cycles of G

## Methods
- [`getCycles(Graph)`](#getcyclesgraph)

## Examples
