# getGenElts
General elements of an ideal cutting down the codimension

- **Package:** [MultiplicitySequence](../../MultiplicitySequence/package/MultiplicitySequence.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/MultiplicitySequence.m2:59:0-59:10`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `MultiplicitySequence$getGenElts`

## Description
This function produces a list of n elements of I whose first j entries generate an ideal of codimension j, for each j from 1 to n. Such general elements underlie the `"genElts"` strategy of [multiplicitySequence](../../MultiplicitySequence/methodFunction/multiplicitySequence.md).

The elements are random combinations of the generators of I, so the output varies between runs; [setRandomSeed](../../Core/methodFunction/setRandomSeed.md) makes it reproducible.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md),
- **n** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the number of general elements to produce

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of n general elements of I

## Options
- **[minTerms](../../MultiplicitySequence/symbol/minTerms.md)** (default: `-1`)
- **[numCandidates](../../MultiplicitySequence/symbol/numCandidates.md)** (default: `3`)

## Methods
- [`getGenElts(Ideal,ZZ)`](#getgeneltsidealzz)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y,z];
```

```macaulay2
I = ideal "xy,yz,zx";
```

```
o2 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
setRandomSeed 0;
 -- setting random seed to 0
```

```macaulay2
getGenElts(I, 2)
      7      7      3     5      7      3
```

```
o4 = {-x*y + -x*z + -y*z, -x*y + -x*z + -y*z}
      9      4      4     6      8      2
o4 : List
```

## Source
```m2
getGenElts = method(Options => {symbol minTerms => -1, symbol numCandidates => 3})
```

## Method details
### `getGenElts(Ideal,ZZ)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/MultiplicitySequence.m2:60:34-84:1`
- **Domain:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Returns:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md) (this method)

#### Source
```m2
getGenElts (Ideal, ZZ) := List => opts -> (I, n) -> (
    G := flatten entries mingens I; -- I_*;
    R := ring I;
    J := ideal(0_R);
    result := {};
    for i from 1 to n do (
        foundNext := false;
        t := if opts.minTerms < 0 then #G else opts.minTerms;
        while not foundNext and t <= #G do (
            if debugLevel > 0 then print("Trying" | (if t > 1 then " sums of " | toString(t) else "") | " generators of I");
            cands := unique apply(opts.numCandidates, i -> (matrix{randomSubset(G, t)} *random(R^t, R^1))_(0,0));
            for c in cands do (
                if codim(saturate(J, I) + ideal c) == i then (
                    result = append(result, c);
                    if member(c, G) then G = delete(c, G);
                    foundNext = true;
                    break;
                );
            );
            t = t+1;
        );
        if foundNext then J = ideal result else error "Could not find general element. Consider running this function again, e.g. with a higher value of minTerms";
    );
    result
)
```

