# inverse2
Inverse of a birational map using a faster algorithm for a special class of maps

- **Package:** [MultiprojectiveVarieties](../../MultiprojectiveVarieties/package/MultiprojectiveVarieties.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/MultiprojectiveVarieties.m2:1893:0-1893:8`
- **Result type:** [MultirationalMap](../../MultiprojectiveVarieties/type/MultirationalMap.md)
- **Aliases:** `MultiprojectiveVarieties$inverse2`

## Description
This assumes that the [graph(MultirationalMap)](graph_lpar_MultirationalMap_rpar_.md) of the input map `Phi` is defined by a simplified system of equations, which may not be true. If the option `Verify` is set to `true`, which is the default choice, then it is verified that the left and right composition of `Phi` with the returned map is the identity, throwing an error if this is not the case.

## Parameters
- **Phi** — a "multi-rational map", a birational map of so-called multi-linear type

## Returns
a "multi-rational map", the inverse map of Phi

## Methods
