# ncMatrix
Create an NCMatrix

- **Package:** [NCAlgebra](../../NCAlgebra/package/NCAlgebra.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NCAlgebra.m2:262:10-262:18`
- **Aliases:** `NCAlgebra$ncMatrix`

## Description
This command creates an NCMatrix.  As with the [matrix](../../Core/methodFunction/matrix.md) command, the user may provide this matrix as a doubly nested list of NCRingElements, or as a doubly nested list of NCMatrices.

The ncMatrix(NCRing, List, List) constructor is used only when creating maps to and from the zero free module.

## Parameters
- **entriesList** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Returns
M, an instance of the type "NCMatrix",

## Methods
- [`ncMatrix(List)`](#ncmatrixlist)
- [`ncMatrix(NCRing,List,List)`](#ncmatrixncringlistlist)

