# gradedReesPiece
Gets a certain degree piece of an ideal in an (extended) Rees algebra

- **Package:** [NonPrincipalTestIdeals](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/package/NonPrincipalTestIdeals.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NonPrincipalTestIdeals.m2:214:0-214:15`
- **Result type:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md)
- **Aliases:** `NonPrincipalTestIdeals$gradedReesPiece`

## Description
Given an ideal $J$ in a Rees ring $T = \oplus T_i$ constructed either with [classicalReesAlgebra](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/methodFunction/classicalReesAlgebra.md) or [extendedReesAlgebra](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/methodFunction/extendedReesAlgebra.md), this will take the $n$th graded piece of $J$ and express it as an ideal in $T_0$.

Note the command [basis](../../Core/methodFunction/basis.md) cannot be used in the extended Rees algebra case as it cannot handle rings with both positive and negative degrees.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), an ideal in an (extended Rees algebra)
- **n** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), a natural number

## Returns
