# reesCanonicalModule
Constructs the graded canonical module in a ring constructed via classicalReesAlgebra or extendedReesAlgebra

- **Package:** [NonPrincipalTestIdeals](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/package/NonPrincipalTestIdeals.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NonPrincipalTestIdeals.m2:78:0-78:19`
- **Result type:** [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md)
- **Aliases:** `NonPrincipalTestIdeals$reesCanonicalModule`

## Description
Computes the graded canonical modules of a ring constructed with [classicalReesAlgebra](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/methodFunction/classicalReesAlgebra.md) or [extendedReesAlgebra](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/methodFunction/extendedReesAlgebra.md) or

The option AmbientCanonical is used to specify the canonical module of `ambient S`.

#### Caveat
One should use this function and not other similar functions to create canonical modules in extended Rees algebras, especially in older versions of Macaulay2.  This is because core Macaulay2 Ext function sometimes gives the wrong answer in rings with variables of negative degrees.  See this github issue [https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/issues/3180](https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/issues/3180)

## Parameters
- **S** — a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), constructed with classicalReesAlgebra or extendedReesAlgebra

## Returns
M, a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), the graded canonical module over S

## Options
- **[AmbientCanonical](../../NonPrincipalTestIdeals/symbol/AmbientCanonical.md)**

## Methods
- [`reesCanonicalModule(Ring)`](#reescanonicalmodulering)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[x,y];
```

```macaulay2
J = ideal(x^2,x*y,y^2);
```

```
o2 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
S = classicalReesAlgebra(J);
```

```macaulay2
T = extendedReesAlgebra(J);
```

```macaulay2
reesCanonicalModule(S)
```

```
o5 = cokernel {1, 3} | -ly_1 ly_0  -y |
              {1, 3} | ly_2  -ly_1 x  |
                            2
o5 : S-module, quotient of S
```

```macaulay2
reesCanonicalModule(T)
```

```
o6 = cokernel {1, 3} | bt_0 -bt_1 -y   x     0     0    -ti 0  |
              {1, 3} | bt_1 -bt_2 0    0     -y    x    0   ti |
              {0, 2} | 0    0     bt_1 -bt_2 -bt_0 bt_1 x   y  |
                            3
o6 : T-module, quotient of T
```

## Source
```m2
reesCanonicalModule = method(Options=>{AmbientCanonical => null})
```

## Method details
### `reesCanonicalModule(Ring)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NonPrincipalTestIdeals.m2:79:39-115:1`
- **Domain:** [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md)
- **Returns:** [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md) (this method)

#### Source
```m2
reesCanonicalModule(Ring) := Module => o->(R1) -> (
	S1 := ambient R1;
	I1 := ideal R1;
	dR := dim R1;
	dS := dim S1;
	varList := first entries vars S1;
	degList := {};
    degSum := 0; --default value 0
    local ambcan;
    if o.AmbientCanonical === null then ( --we do things slightly weirdly for extended Rees algebras.
        if (R1#?"ExtendedReesAlgebra") and (R1#"ExtendedReesAlgebra") then (
            varList = select(varList, z -> ((degree z)#0 >= 0));--grab variables with positive initial degree
            degList = apply(varList, q -> (degree(q))); --grab their degrees next
            --print degList;
            degSum = -(sum degList)+{1,0};  --we do a shift for t^{-1} variable
        )
        else if (#varList > 0) then ( --then there are some variables
            if (#(degree(varList#0)) == 1) then (
                degList = apply(varList, q -> (degree(q))#0); )
            else (
                degList = apply(varList, q -> (degree(q))); );
            degSum = -(sum degList);
        );
        if (debugLevel > 1) then (
            print degList;
            print degSum;
        );
        ambcan = S1^{degSum}; 
    )
    else (
        ambcan = o.AmbientCanonical;
        --print (degrees ambcan);
    );    
    --print "doing classical Ext";
    --M1 := (Ext^(dS - dR)(S1^1/I1, ambcan))**R1
    M1 := (manualExt(dS - dR,S1^1/I1, ambcan))**R1
)
```

