# gateHomotopy
Homotopy implemented via straight line programs

- **Package:** [NumericalAlgebraicGeometry](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/package/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/extraNAGtypes.m2:247:0-247:12`
- **Aliases:** `NumericalAlgebraicGeometry$gateHomotopy`

## Description
Optional arguments:[Software](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Software.md)-- specifies how the homotopy is evaluated: `(M2, M2engine)`

#### Caveat
The order of inputs for unexported internal evaluation functions (evaluateH, etc.) is fixed as follows: `Parameters, X, T`.

## Parameters
- **H** — an instance of the type "GateMatrix", a family of systems (given by a column vector)
- **T** — an instance of the type "InputGate", homotopy (continuation) parameter
- **X** — an instance of the type "GateMatrix", (a row vector of) variables

## Returns
HS,; an instance of the type "GateHomotopy" or an instance of the type "GateParameterHomotopy", a homotopy that can be used with some routines of "NumericalAlgebraicGeometry"

## Options
- **[Parameters](../../RandomMonomialIdeals/symbol/Parameters.md)** — specifies parameter names
- **[Software](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Software.md)** — specifies where evaluation should be done (M2=top level, M2engine=core)
- **[Strategy](../../Core/symbol/Strategy.md)** — strategy is either to \ (default: `compress`)

