# solveSystem
Solve a system of polynomial equations

- **Package:** [NumericalAlgebraicGeometry](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/package/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/0-dim-methods.m2:12:0-12:11`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `NumericalAlgebraicGeometry$solveSystem`

## Description
Solve a system of polynomial equations using homotopy continuation methods.

The system is assumed to have finitely many solutions. If it is not square (number of equations = number of variables), [squareUp](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/squareUp.md) is applied and solutions to the original system are then picked out from the resulting (larger) set of solutions.

The output (produced by [track](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/track.md) with default options) contains all [Point](../../NAGtypes/type/Point.md) obtained at the end of homotopy paths when tracking starting at the [totalDegreeStartSystem](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/totalDegreeStartSystem.md). In particular, this means that solving a system that has fewer than Bezout bound many solutions will produce points that are not marked as regular. See [track](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/track.md) for detailed examples.

## Parameters
- **F** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), contains polynomials with complex coefficients

## Returns
s, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), contains all complex solutions to the system F=0

## Options
- **[PostProcess](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/PostProcess.md)** — specifies whether to postprocess the solutions (default: `true`)
- **[Precision](../../Core/symbol/Precision.md)**
- **[Software](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Software.md)**
- **[gamma](../../PHCpack/symbol/gamma.md)**
- **[tDegree](../../PHCpack/symbol/tDegree.md)**
- **[tStep](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/tStep.md)**
- **[tStepMin](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/tStepMin.md)**
- **[stepIncreaseFactor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/stepIncreaseFactor.md)**
- **[numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease.md)**
- **[Predictor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Predictor.md)**
- **[maxCorrSteps](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/maxCorrSteps.md)**
- **[CorrectorTolerance](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/CorrectorTolerance.md)**
- **[EndZoneFactor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/EndZoneFactor.md)**
- **[InfinityThreshold](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/InfinityThreshold.md)**
- **[SingularConditionNumber](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/SingularConditionNumber.md)**
- **[ResidualTolerance](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/ResidualTolerance.md)**
- **[Normalize](../../QuaternaryQuartics/symbol/Normalize.md)**
- **[Projectivize](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Projectivize.md)**

## Methods
- [`solveSystem(List)`](#solvesystemlist)
- [`solveSystem(PolySystem)`](#solvesystempolysystem)

## Examples
