# track
Track a linear segment homotopy given start and target system

- **Package:** [NumericalAlgebraicGeometry](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/package/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/track.m2:37:0-37:5`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `NumericalAlgebraicGeometry$track`

## Description
Polynomial homotopy continuation techniques are used to obtain solutions of the target system given a start system. For an introduction to the subject see A. J. Sommese, J. Verschelde, and C. W. Wampler, "Introduction to numerical algebraic geometry", in "Solving polynomial equations" (2005), 301--338A. J. Sommese and C. W. Wampler, "The numerical solution of systems of polynomials", World Scientific Publishing (2005)The package implements a most commonly used homotopy: H(t) = \gamma t^d T + (1-t)^d S

where S and T are square systems (number of equations = number of variables) of polynomials over [CC](../../Core/type/CC.md), t is in the interval [0,1] and d = [tDegree](../../PHCpack/symbol/tDegree.md). Here is an example with regular solutions at the ends of all homotopy paths:

Another outcome of tracking a path is divergence (established heuristically). In that case the divergent paths are marked with an `I` ([AbstractPoint](../../NAGtypes/type/AbstractPoint.md) is set to [Infinity](../../NAGtypes/symbol/Infinity.md)).

Some divergent paths as well as most of the paths ending in singular (multiplicity>1) or near-singular (clustered) solutions are marked with an `M` ([AbstractPoint](../../NAGtypes/type/AbstractPoint.md) is set to [MinStepFailure](../../NAGtypes/symbol/MinStepFailure.md)).

Tracking in the projective space uses the homotopy corresponding to an arc of a great circle on  a unit sphere in the space of homogeneous polynomial systems of a fixed degree. In particular, this is done for certified homotopy tracking (see C. Beltran and A. Leykin, "Certified numerical homotopy tracking", Experimental Mathematics 21(1): 69-83 (2012)):

Note that the projective tracker is invoked either if the target system is a homogeneous system or if [Projectivize](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Projectivize.md)`=>true` is specified.

#### Caveat
Predictor=>Certified works only with (Software=>M2 or Software=>M2engine) and Normalize=>true. Unspecified optional arguments (with default values [null](../../Core/object/null.md)) have their actual values taken from a local hashtable of defaults controlled by the functions [getDefault](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/getDefault.md) and [setDefault](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/methodFunction/setDefault.md).

## Parameters
- **S** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), contains the polynomials in the start system
- **solsS** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), contains start solutions
- **T** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), contains the polynomials in the target system

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), solsT is a list of "points" that are solutions of T=0 obtained by continuing solsS of S=0

## Options
- **[Software](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Software.md)**
- **[NoOutput](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/NoOutput.md)**
- **[gamma](../../PHCpack/symbol/gamma.md)**
- **[tDegree](../../PHCpack/symbol/tDegree.md)**
- **[tStep](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/tStep.md)**
- **[tStepMin](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/tStepMin.md)**
- **[stepIncreaseFactor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/stepIncreaseFactor.md)**
- **[numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/numberSuccessesBeforeIncrease.md)**
- **[Predictor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Predictor.md)**
- **[SLPpredictor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/SLPpredictor.md)**
- **[MultistepDegree](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/MultistepDegree.md)**
- **[SLPcorrector](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/SLPcorrector.md)**
- **[maxCorrSteps](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/maxCorrSteps.md)**
- **[CorrectorTolerance](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/CorrectorTolerance.md)**
- **[EndZoneFactor](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/EndZoneFactor.md)**
- **[InfinityThreshold](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/InfinityThreshold.md)**
- **[SingularConditionNumber](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/SingularConditionNumber.md)**
- **[Normalize](../../QuaternaryQuartics/symbol/Normalize.md)**
- **[Projectivize](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Projectivize.md)**
