# certifyDistinctSolutions
Determine whether given points are distinct approximate solutions to the system

- **Package:** [NumericalCertification](../../NumericalCertification/package/NumericalCertification.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalCertification.m2:214:0-214:24`
- **Aliases:** `NumericalCertification$certifyDistinctSolutions`

## Description
This function executes the gamma test based on the value computed by [computeConstants](../../NumericalCertification/methodFunction/computeConstants.md), and determine whether given points are distinct or not.

However, if two solutions are too close, it concludes that inputs are not distinct.

Even worse, if two solutions are close enough and both have alpha value which are bigger than $0.03$, it gives indecisive comments.

In this case, user should apply [newton](../../Units/object/newton.md) to the point to get more precise approximation.

