# optimizeNelderMead
Samples a real point on a variety

- **Package:** [NumericalImplicitization](../../NumericalImplicitization/package/NumericalImplicitization.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalImplicitization/approxPoint.m2:6:13-6:31`
- **Aliases:** `NumericalImplicitization$optimizeNelderMead`

## Description
This method samples a real point on a variety numerically, using a combination of the [Nelder-Mead simplex method](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelder%E2%80%93Mead_method) and [line search](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Line_search) with gradient descent. This can be much quicker than performing a numerical irreducible decomposition.

The option `Tolerance` specifies a requested error tolerance for the point, with respect to the generating set of the ideal.

The option `Iterations` specifies an upper limit on the number of iterations to run the approximation algorithms. If this value is too low, then the method will return a point which may not be within the specified error tolerance.

The following example shows how to sample a point from the 4 x 5 funtf variety.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), specifying a source variety $V(I)$

## Returns
an instance of the type "Point", a sample real point on $V(I)$

## Options
- **[Tolerance](../../SlackIdeals/symbol/Tolerance.md)** (default: `.000001`)
- **[Iterations](../../NumericalAlgebraicGeometry/symbol/Iterations.md)** (default: `200`)
- **[Initial](../../NumericalImplicitization/symbol/Initial.md)** (default: `standard`)

## Methods
- [`optimizeNelderMead(FunctionClosure,List)`](#optimizeneldermeadfunctionclosurelist)
- [`optimizeNelderMead(Ideal)`](#optimizeneldermeadideal)

## Examples
