# def1
Degrees of a basis of T^1

- **Package:** [NumericalSemigroups](../../NumericalSemigroups/package/NumericalSemigroups.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NumericalSemigroups.m2:1012:0-1012:4`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `NumericalSemigroups$def1`

## Description
T^1(B) is the tangent space to the versal deformaion of the ring B, and is finite dimensional when B has isolated singularity. If B = S/I is a Cohen presentation, then T^1(B) = coker Hom(Omega_S, B) -> Hom(I/I^2, B). When B is a semigroup ring, then Henry Pinkham proved that an open subset of the space of elements of T1 of negative degree correspond to smoothings of the projective cone of the semigroup ring to Riemann surfaces

## Parameters
- **L** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), generators of a semigroup

## Returns
D, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), degrees of a basis of T^1(semigroupRing L)

## Options
- **[BaseField](../../WeierstrassSemigroups/symbol/BaseField.md)** (default: `ZZ/101`)
- **[JustDegs](JustDegs.md)** (default: `true`)

## Methods
- [`def1(List)`](#def1list)

## Examples
```macaulay2
def1{2,3}
```

```
o1 = {-6, -4}
o1 : List
```

