# oiSyz
Compute a Gröbner basis for the syzygy module of a submodule of a free OI-module

- **Package:** [OIGroebnerBases](../../OIGroebnerBases/package/OIGroebnerBases.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/OIGroebnerBases.m2:921:0-921:5`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `OIGroebnerBases$oiSyz`

## Description
Given a non-empty Gröbner basis `G` for a submodule $\mathbf{M}$ of a free OI-module $\mathbf{F}$, this method computes a Gröbner basis $G'$ for the syzygy module of $\mathbf{M}$ with respect to the Schreyer order induced by $G$; see [OIMonomialOrder](../../OIGroebnerBases/symbol/OIMonomialOrder.md).

The new Gröbner basis $G'$ lives in an appropriate free OI-module $\mathbf{G}$ with basis symbol `d` whose basis elements are mapped onto the elements of $G$ by a canonical surjective map $\varphi:\mathbf{G}\to\mathbf{M}$ (see Definition 4.1 of [1]). Moreover, the degrees of the basis elements of $\mathbf{G}$ are automatically shifted to coincide with the degrees of the elements of $G$, so that $\varphi$ is homogeneous if $G$ consists of homogeneous elements. If $G'$ is not empty, then one obtains $\mathbf{G}$ by applying [getFreeOIModule](../../OIGroebnerBases/methodFunction/getFreeOIModule.md) to any element of $G'$. One obtains $\varphi$ by using [getSchreyerMap](../../OIGroebnerBases/methodFunction/getSchreyerMap.md).

The [Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md) option must be either `true` or `false`, depending on whether one wants debug information printed.

The [Strategy](../../Core/symbol/Strategy.md) option has the following permissible values:

`Strategy => ``[FastNonminimal](../../Core/symbol/FastNonminimal.md)` for no post-processing of the basis`Strategy => ``[Minimize](../../Core/symbol/Minimize.md)` to minimize the basis after it is computed; see [minimizeOIGB](../../OIGroebnerBases/methodFunction/minimizeOIGB.md)`Strategy => ``[Reduce](../../Core/symbol/Reduce.md)` to reduce the basis after it is computed; see [reduceOIGB](../../OIGroebnerBases/methodFunction/reduceOIGB.md)References:

[1] M. Morrow and U. Nagel, Computing Gröbner Bases and Free Resolutions of OI-Modules, Preprint, arXiv:2303.06725, 2023.

## Parameters
- **d** — a [Symbol](../../Core/type/Symbol.md),
- **G** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)
- **[Strategy](../../Core/symbol/Strategy.md)** (default: `Minimize`)

## Methods
- [`oiSyz(List,Symbol)`](#oisyzlistsymbol)

## Examples
