# mixedVolume
Computes mixed volume of a polynomial system

- **Package:** [PHCpack](../../PHCpack/package/PHCpack.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/PHCpack.m2:899:0-899:11`
- **Aliases:** `PHCpack$mixedVolume`

## Description
The mixed volume of a polynomial system $S:=\{f_1,\dots, f_n\}$ is defined as follows: Let $P_1,\dots, P_n$ be the Newton polytopes of $f_1,\dots, f_n$, i.e., $P_i$ is the convex hull of the exponents of the monomials in the support of $f_i$. The mixed volume of $S$ is $$ \sum_{1\leq h\leq n} \sum_{1\leq i_1\dots\leq i_h\leq n} (-1)^{n-h}V_n(P_{i_1}+\dots+P_{i_h}), $$ where $V_n$ denotes the $n$-dimensional Euclidean volume.

Bernstein's theorem (D. N. Bernstein, The number of roots of a system of equations, Functional. Anal. Appl 9 (1975), no. 3, 183-185), a generalization of the classical Bezout's theorem, shows that for a zero-dimensional system, the mixed volume provides an upper bound on the number of complex isolated roots. If the coefficients of the system are sufficiently generic, the mixed volume is a sharp bound.

Note that only those solutions with nonzero components are shown, even if StableMixedVolume is true.  See the end of the temporary output file for the solutions with zero components.

The method `mixedVolume` calls an Ada translation of ACM TOMS Algorithm 846: MixedVol: a software package for mixed-volume computation by Tangan Gao, T. Y. Li, Mengnien Wu, [ACM TOMS](http://portal.acm.org/citation.cfm?doid=1114268.1114274) 31(4):555-560, 2005.

#### Consequences
Writes the system to temporary filesInvokes the command `phc -m` (with option 4)Stores output of phc in temporary fileParses and outputs the solutions.

## Parameters
- **S** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), whose entries are the polynomials of a square system

## Returns
mv, an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the mixed volume of the system S; sv, an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the stable mixed volume of the system S; q, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), whose entries are polynomials in a random coefficient system, used as a start system for the homotopy; qSols, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), whose entries are solutions of the start system q

## Options
- **[StableMixedVolume](../../PHCpack/symbol/StableMixedVolume.md)** — optional input for computation of the stable mixed volume (default: `false`)
- **[StartSystem](../../PHCpack/symbol/StartSystem.md)** — optional input for computation of mixed volume by solving a random coefficient system (default: `false`)
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** — option to specify whether additional output is wanted (default: `false`)
- **[numThreads](../../PHCpack/symbol/numThreads.md)** — option to set the number of threads when solving a start system (default: `0`)
- **[interactive](../../PHCpack/symbol/interactive.md)** — option to switch to the interactive mode of phc -m (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`mixedVolume(List)`](#mixedvolumelist)

## Examples
