# rationalPointOnConic
Rational point on a conic.

- **Package:** [Parametrization](../../Parametrization/package/Parametrization.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Parametrization.m2:452:3-452:23`
- **Result type:** [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md)
- **Aliases:** `Parametrization$rationalPointOnConic`

## Description
Decides whether a conic has a rational point and if so computes one.

#### Caveat
Returns the 0-matrix if there is no rational point.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), the ideal of an irreducible conic.

## Returns
a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a row matrix over \mathbb{Q} with homogeneous integer coordinates of a rational point on the conic or 0-matrix if there is none.

## Options
- **[vb](../../Parametrization/symbol/vb.md)** (default: `0`)

## Methods
- [`rationalPointOnConic(Ideal)`](#rationalpointonconicideal)

