# dualPieriColumn
GL-equivariant projection wedge^d V ⊗ S_lambda V --> S_mu V

- **Package:** [PieriMaps](../../PieriMaps/package/PieriMaps.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/PieriMaps.m2:1595:0-1595:15`
- **Result type:** [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md)
- **Aliases:** `PieriMaps$dualPieriColumn`

## Description
Column-form analogue of [dualPieri](../../PieriMaps/methodFunction/dualPieri.md): the $GL_n$-equivariant projection from $\wedge^d V \otimes S_\lambda V$ onto the chosen $S_\mu V$ summand (unique up to scalar).  Construction stacks [pieriColumn](../../PieriMaps/methodFunction/pieriColumn.md) inclusions for every addable vertical $d$-strip and inverts.

## Parameters
- **cols** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of column indices recording the strip $\mu/\lambda$
- **mu** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), the target shape: $\mu = \lambda + (\text{vertical $d$-strip})$ with $d = \#\mathrm{cols}$
- **P** — a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md), a SkewCommutative ring ($\wedge^d V$ is encoded there)

## Returns
a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a $K$-matrix of size $\dim S_\mu V \times \bigl(\dim S_\lambda V \cdot \binom{n}{d}\bigr)$. Columns indexed by $(T_\lambda, \alpha)$ pairs ($\alpha$ an exterior monomial).

## Options
- **[Convention](../../PieriMaps/symbol/Convention.md)** (default: `Filling`)

## Methods
- [`dualPieriColumn(List,List,PolynomialRing)`](#dualpiericolumnlistlistpolynomialring)

## Examples
```macaulay2
P = QQ[e_0..e_2, SkewCommutative => true];
```

```macaulay2
M = pieriColumn({2,1}, {1}, P);
             6      8
```

```
o2 : Matrix P  <-- P
```

```macaulay2
N = dualPieriColumn({2,1}, {1}, P);
              8       18
```

```
o3 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ
```

```macaulay2
numRows N, numColumns N
```

```
o4 = (8, 18)
o4 : Sequence
```

## Source
```m2
dualPieriColumn = method(Options => {Convention => "Filling"})
```

