# projectiveFatPoints
Produces the ideal and initial ideal from the coordinates of a finite set of fat points

- **Package:** [Points](../../Points/package/Points.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Points.m2:496:0-496:19`
- **Aliases:** `Points$projectiveFatPoints`

## Description
This function uses a modified Buchberger-Moeller algorithm to compute a grobner basis for the ideal of a finite number of fat points in projective space.

#### Caveat
For small sets of points and/or multiplicities, this method might be slower than [projectiveFatPointsByIntersection](../../Points/methodFunction/projectiveFatPointsByIntersection.md).

## Parameters
- **M** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), in which each column consists of the projective coordinates of a point
- **mults** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), in which each element determines the multiplicity of the corresponding point
- **R** — a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), homogeneous coordinate ring of the projective space containing the points

## Returns
inG, an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), initial ideal of the set of fat points; G, a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), list of generators for Grobner basis for ideal of fat points

## Options
- **[VerifyPoints](../../Points/symbol/VerifyPoints.md)** — Option to projectiveFatPoints. (default: `true`)

## Methods
- [`projectiveFatPoints(Matrix,List,Ring)`](#projectivefatpointsmatrixlistring)

## Examples
