# statePolytope
Computes the state polytope of a homogeneous ideal

- **Package:** [Polyhedra](../../Polyhedra/package/Polyhedra.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Polyhedra/extended/not_refactored.m2:12:0-12:13`
- **Result type:** [Polyhedron](../../Polyhedra/type/Polyhedron.md)
- **Aliases:** `Polyhedra$statePolytope`

## Description
A `statePolytope` of an Ideal `I` has as normalFan the Groebner fan of the ideal. We use the construction by Sturmfels, see Algorithm 3.2 in [Bernd Sturmfels'](http://math.berkeley.edu/~bernd/index.html) Groebner Bases and Convex Polytopes, volume 8 of University Lecture Series. American Mathematical Society, first edition, 1995.

Consider the following ideal in a ring with 3 variables:

The state polytope of this ideal is a triangle in 3 space, because the ideal has three initial ideals:

The generators of the three initial ideals are given in the first part of the result.

## Parameters
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), which must be homogeneous

## Returns
P, a [Polyhedron](../../Polyhedra/type/Polyhedron.md)

## Methods
- [`statePolytope(Ideal)`](#statepolytopeideal)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[a,b,c]
```

```
o1 = R
o1 : PolynomialRing
```

```macaulay2
I = ideal (a-b,a-c,b-c)
```

```
o2 = ideal (a - b, a - c, b - c)
o2 : Ideal of R
```

```macaulay2
statePolytope I
```

```
o3 = ({| b a |, | c b |, | c a |}, Polyhedron{...1...})
o3 : Sequence
```

## Source
