# texPoset
Generates a string containing a TikZ-figure of a poset

- **Package:** [Posets](../../Posets/package/Posets.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Posets.m2:1144:10-1144:18`
- **Result type:** [String](../../Core/type/String.md)
- **Aliases:** `Posets$texPoset`

## Description
This method creates a TikZ-figure of the Hasse diagram of the given poset which can be included in a LaTeX file.  The representation places the vertices on horizontal lines corresponding to the [filtration](../../ToricVectorBundles/methodFunction/filtration.md) of the poset.  The only displayed edges are the [coveringRelations](../../Posets/methodFunction/coveringRelations.md) which are oriented so that lower vertices less than higher vertices.

The method attempts to display labels in a sane way, if they are not suppressed by the `SuppressLabels` option. Note that the `SuppressLabels` option's default value can be set in the "~/. Macaulay2/init-Posets.m2" file.

Further, sometimes the vertices of the poset line up in unfortunate ways that causes edges to touch other vertices.  Using the `Jitter` option can relieve this by adding a small random horizontal shift to each vertex.

#### Caveat
Calling texPoset via the command [tex](../../Core/methodFunction/tex.md) expects that no options are given.

## Parameters
- **P** — an instance of the type "Poset",

## Returns
S, a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), a TikZ-figure of $P$

## Options
- **[SuppressLabels](../../Posets/symbol/SuppressLabels.md)** (default: `true`)
- **[Jitter](../../Posets/symbol/Jitter.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`texPoset(Poset)`](#texposetposet)

## Examples
```macaulay2
texPoset booleanLattice 2
```

```
o1 = \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1, vertices/.style={draw, fill=black, circle, inner sep=0pt}]
             \node [vertices] (0) at (-0+0,0){};
             \node [vertices] (1) at (-.75+0,1.33333){};
             \node [vertices] (2) at (-.75+1.5,1.33333){};
             \node [vertices] (3) at (-0+0,2.66667){};
     \foreach \to/\from in {0/1, 2/3, 0/2, 1/3}
     \draw [-] (\to)--(\from);
     \end{tikzpicture}
```

```macaulay2
texPoset(booleanLattice 2, Jitter => true)
```

```
o2 = \begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1, vertices/.style={draw, fill=black, circle, inner sep=0pt}]
             \node [vertices] (0) at (-0+.267814,0){};
             \node [vertices] (1) at (-.75+.202018,1.33333){};
             \node [vertices] (2) at (-.75+1.58819,1.33333){};
             \node [vertices] (3) at (-0+.189883,2.66667){};
     \foreach \to/\from in {0/1, 2/3, 0/2, 1/3}
     \draw [-] (\to)--(\from);
     \end{tikzpicture}
```

