# qthConductor
Computes a conductor element which also lives in the given Noether normalization, P

- **Package:** [QthPower](../../QthPower/package/QthPower.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/QthPower.m2:292:0-292:12`
- **Result type:** [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md)
- **Aliases:** `QthPower$qthConductor`

## Description
This gives a canonical conductor element {	t delta} living in the given Noether normalization, P, the subring of the last numRows(wtR) (free) variables.

## Parameters
- **depno** — number of dependent variables
- **I** — ideal of relations

## Returns
