# changeVar
Computes a change of variables which make the first entry of a unimodular row monic in a specified variable

- **Package:** [QuillenSuslin](../../QuillenSuslin/package/QuillenSuslin.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/QuillenSuslin.m2:677:0-677:9`
- **Result type:** [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md)
- **Aliases:** `QuillenSuslin$changeVar`

## Description
The purpose of changeVar is to compute a unimodular matrix `A` and an invertible change of variables (given as a matrix `B` with the inverse change of variables given by `C`) so that after multiplying the given unimodular row `U` by `A` and applying the substitution `B` (with `sub(U*A, B)`), the first entry of the new row becomes monic in the last variable in the list `L`.

This method is primarily used before applying [horrocks](../../QuillenSuslin/methodFunction/horrocks.md), since horrocks requires the first entry of the unimodular row to be monic in the given variable.

Notice that after multiplying `U` by the unimodular matrix `A` and applying the change of variables `B` (using the [substitute](../../Core/methodFunction/substitute.md) command), the first entry in `U'` above is now monic in `x`.

The order of the variables given in the list matter, as changeVar will construct a change of variable so that the new unimodular row is monic in the last variable of the list.

In the next example, since we are using the command `changeVar(U,{x, y})` the first entry in the row `sub(U*A, B)` will be monic in `y`.

One can also check that the inverse change of variables, `C`, will give the matrix `U*A`, undoing the change of variables given by `B`.

## Parameters
- **L** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), the variables appearing in the matrix, ordered so that the first entry of the new row will become monic in the last variable in the list
- **U** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a unimodular row

## Returns
A, a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a unimodular matrix that when multiplied by the row will make the first entry monic after the change of variables; B, a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), change of variables; C, a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), inverse change of variables

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `0`)

## Methods
- [`changeVar(Matrix,List)`](#changevarmatrixlist)

