# realRootIsolation
A list that isolates the real roots of a univariate polynomial with rational coefficients

- **Package:** [RealRoots](../../RealRoots/package/RealRoots.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/RealRoots.m2:395:0-395:17`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `RealRoots$realRootIsolation`

## Description
This computes disjoint intervals of length at most `r`, each containing exactly one real root of `f`.

## Parameters
- **f** — a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md), a univariate polynomial with rational coefficients
- **r** — a [QQ](../../Core/type/QQ.md), a positive rational number

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of disjoint intervals

## Methods
- [`realRootIsolation(RingElement,ZZ)`](#realrootisolationringelementzz)
- [`realRootIsolation(RingElement,QQ)`](#realrootisolationringelementqq)

## Examples
```macaulay2
R = QQ[t]
```

