# canCurveWithFixedScroll
Computes a g-nodal canonical curve with a degree k line bundle on a normalized scroll

- **Package:** [RelativeCanonicalResolution](../../RelativeCanonicalResolution/package/RelativeCanonicalResolution.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/RelativeCanonicalResolution.m2:175:2-175:25`
- **Result type:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md)
- **Aliases:** `RelativeCanonicalResolution$canCurveWithFixedScroll`

## Description
This function computes the ideal of a g-nodal canonical curve with a degree k<g line bundle that lies on a normalized scroll. The construction of such curves is based on the Macaulay2 package  [kGonalNodalCurves](http://www.math.uni-sb.de/ag/schreyer/index.php/people/researchers/75-christian-bopp)

## Parameters
- **g** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the genus of the curve
- **k** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the degree of the line bundle on C
- **n** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the integer defining the characteristic p ($\ge n$) of the ground field

## Returns
ICan, an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), the ideal of the canonical curve

## Methods
- [`canCurveWithFixedScroll(ZZ,ZZ,ZZ)`](#cancurvewithfixedscrollzzzzzz)

## Examples
```macaulay2
(g,k,n) = (8,5,1000);
```

```macaulay2
Ican = canCurveWithFixedScroll(g,k,n);
               ZZ
```

```
o2 : Ideal of ----[t ..t ]
              1009  0   7
```

```macaulay2
genus Ican, degree Ican, dim Ican
```

```
o3 = (8, 14, 2)
o3 : Sequence
```

```macaulay2
betti res(Ican, DegreeLimit => 1)
            0  1  2  3
```

```
o4 = total: 1 15 35 21
         0: 1  .  .  .
         1: . 15 35 21
o4 : BettiTally
```

```macaulay2
Phi = matrix{{t_0,t_2,t_4,t_6},{t_1,t_3,t_5,t_7}}
```

```
o5 = | t_0 t_2 t_4 t_6 |
     | t_1 t_3 t_5 t_7 |
              ZZ          2       ZZ          4
o5 : Matrix (----[t ..t ])  <-- (----[t ..t ])
             1009  0   7         1009  0   7
```

```macaulay2
Iscroll = minors(2,Phi);
               ZZ
```

```
o6 : Ideal of ----[t ..t ]
              1009  0   7
```

```macaulay2
Ican + Iscroll == Ican
```

```
o7 = true
```

