# colorfulPresentation
A presentation of the Stanley-Reisner ring of the barycentric subdivision of a simplicial complex over its colorful parameter ring

- **Package:** [ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings](../../ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings/package/ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings.m2:134:0-134:20`
- **Result type:** [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md)
- **Aliases:** `ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings$colorfulPresentation`

## Description
Since the barycentric subdivision of a simplicial complex `D` is a balanced simplicial complex `B`, i.e., there exists a `dim(D)+1` proper vertex coloring, this `colorfulPresentation` takes in the barycentric subdivision of a simplicial complex, computes a colorful system of parameters for the Stanley-Reisner ring of `B` and then returns this quotient ring as an N-graded module over the colorful parameter ring.

## Parameters
- **D** — an "abstract simplicial complex",
- **F** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), A list of facets defining a simplicial complex D

## Returns
a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), A graded presentation of the Stanley-Reisner ring over its universal parameter ring

## Methods
- [`colorfulPresentation(SimplicialComplex)`](#colorfulpresentationsimplicialcomplex)
- [`colorfulPresentation(List)`](#colorfulpresentationlist)

## Examples
