# simplex
Simplex in the variables of a polynomial ring.

- **Package:** [SRdeformations](../../SRdeformations/package/SRdeformations.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SRdeformations.m2:1696:0-1696:7`
- **Aliases:** `SRdeformations$simplex`

## Description
Returns a simplex on the variables of R.

If R does not have a coker grading then the standard projective space fan rays are added, see [addCokerGrading](../../SRdeformations/methodFunction/addCokerGrading.md) and [raysPPn](../../SRdeformations/methodFunction/raysPPn.md).

The Option computeFaces=>false suppresses the computation of all faces.

If Rdual is specified it is used for the vertices of the dual simplex, if not a new polynomial ring is created. It is graded by the coordinates of the vertices of the dual simplex.

The dual simplex is always created without face data.

## Parameters
- **R** — a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md),
- **Rdual** — a [PolynomialRing](../../Core/type/PolynomialRing.md),

## Returns
an "embedded complex",

## Options
- **[computeFaces](../../SRdeformations/symbol/computeFaces.md)**

## Methods
- [`simplex(PolynomialRing)`](#simplexpolynomialring)
- [`simplex(PolynomialRing,PolynomialRing)`](#simplexpolynomialringpolynomialring)

