# SVDHomology
Estimate the homology of a chain complex over RR with the SVD decomposition

- **Package:** [SVDComplexes](../../SVDComplexes/package/SVDComplexes.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SVDComplexes.m2:309:0-309:11`
- **Result type:** [HashTable](../../Core/type/HashTable.md)
- **Aliases:** `SVDComplexes$SVDHomology`

## Description
We compute the singular value decomposition either by the iterated Projections or by the Laplacian method. In case of the projection method we record in h1 the last two nonzero singular values and first singular value expected to be really zero.

In case of the Laplacian method we record in h1 the smallest common Eigenvalues of the neighboring Laplacians, and the first Eigenvalue expected to be zero.

In case the input consists of two chain complexes we use the iterated  Projection method, and identify the stable singular values.

#### Caveat
The algorithm might fail if the condition numbers of the differential are too bad

## Parameters
- **C** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), over RR_{53}
- **C'** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), in a lower precision

## Returns
h, a [HashTable](../../Core/type/HashTable.md), the dimensions of the homology groups HH C; h1, a [HashTable](../../Core/type/HashTable.md), information about the singular values

## Methods
- [`SVDHomology(Complex)`](#svdhomologycomplex)
- [`SVDHomology(Complex,Complex)`](#svdhomologycomplexcomplex)

