# inclusion
Build the freest possible inclusion map

- **Package:** [Schubert2](../../Schubert2/package/Schubert2.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Schubert2.m2:1313:0-1313:9`
- **Aliases:** `Schubert2$inclusion`

## Description
Given the pullback map `f` from `A` to `B`, builds the freest possible extension `E` of `A` by `B` (see [extensionAlgebra](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/extensionAlgebra.md)), and then adds appropriate metadata to make the maps from `E` to `B` and vice-versa into an [AbstractVarietyMap](../../Schubert2/type/AbstractVarietyMap.md).  Enough information must be given to compute the dimensions of `X` and `Y`, either by using the SubDimension, SuperDimension, and Codimension options, or by having varieties already attached to `A` and/or `B`.  Likewise, enough information must be given to compute the tangent classes of `X` and `Y`.

This construction is useful for computations where the pullback map is known but the pushforward is either not known or cannot be defined.

#### Consequences
An [extensionAlgebra](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/extensionAlgebra.md) of `A` by `B` is built, with normal class equal to the degree-`r` part of `c`.  This algebra is made into the ring of a variety `Z`, see [abstractVariety](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/abstractVariety.md).  A tangent class is installed on `Z`, see [tangentBundle](../../ToricVectorBundles/methodFunction/tangentBundle.md).  If `A` and `B` each have an [integral](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/integral.md) defined, then an integral is defined on the coordinate ring of `Z`, and a [StructureMap](../../Schubert2/symbol/StructureMap.md) is installed on `Z`. A variety `X` for `B` is built if `B` is not already the ring of a variety, see [abstractVariety](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/abstractVariety.md).  A tangent class is installed on `X` if it does not already have one, see [tangentBundle](../../ToricVectorBundles/methodFunction/tangentBundle.md).  A [StructureMap](../../Schubert2/symbol/StructureMap.md) is installed if `B` already has an [integral](../../Schubert2/methodFunction/integral.md) defined. If `Base` option is used, the supplied ring is made into the ring of a variety, if it is not already one.

## Parameters
- **f** — from A to B; we think of A as part of the Chow ring of Y and B as part of the Chow ring of X

## Returns
an "abstract variety map", the natural map from X to Z.

## Options
- **[SubDimension](../../Schubert2/symbol/SubDimension.md)**
- **[SuperDimension](../../Schubert2/symbol/SuperDimension.md)**
- **[Codimension](../../Schubert2/symbol/Codimension.md)**
- **[SubTangent](../../Schubert2/symbol/SubTangent.md)**
- **[SuperTangent](../../Schubert2/symbol/SuperTangent.md)**
- **[NormalClass](../../Schubert2/symbol/NormalClass.md)**
- **[Base](../../Core/symbol/Base.md)**

## Methods
- [`inclusion(RingMap)`](#inclusionringmap)

