# mRegular
MRegular(F,G) computes the regularity of F with respect to G (globally generated), in the sense of Castelnuovo-Mumford.  Omitting G assumes G=O_X(1).

- **Package:** [SectionRing](../../SectionRing/package/SectionRing.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SectionRing.m2:116:0-116:8`
- **Result type:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Aliases:** `SectionRing$mRegular`

## Description
MRegular(F, G) utilizes a binary search to compute the smallest m such that F is m-regular with respect to G, utilizing the function isMRegular.  mRegular(I) computes the regularity of O_X(D), where D is the associated divisor to I.

## Parameters
- **F** — a [CoherentSheaf](../../Varieties/type/CoherentSheaf.md),
- **G** — a [CoherentSheaf](../../Varieties/type/CoherentSheaf.md),

## Returns
an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md),

## Methods
- [`mRegular(CoherentSheaf,CoherentSheaf)`](#mregularcoherentsheafcoherentsheaf)
- [`mRegular(CoherentSheaf)`](#mregularcoherentsheaf)
- [`mRegular(Ideal)`](#mregularideal)

## Source
```m2
