# intersectionProduct
A class in the Chow ring of the ambient space representing the Fulton-MacPherson intersection product of two schemes inside a variety

- **Package:** [SegreClasses](../../SegreClasses/package/SegreClasses.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SegreClasses.m2:480:0-480:19`
- **Result type:** [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md)
- **Aliases:** `SegreClasses$intersectionProduct`

## Description
For subschemes X, V of a smooth complete intersection subvariety Y of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} this command computes the Fulton-MacPherson intersection product of X with V in Y as a class in the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. Note that this command requires that Y is a smooth complete intersection subvariety, however this is not checked internally.

## Parameters
- **A** — a [QuotientRing](../../Core/type/QuotientRing.md), the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. This ring can be built by applying "makeChowRing" to the coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
- **IV** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a multi-homogeneous ideal defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; "makeProductRing" builds the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
- **IX** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a multi-homogeneous ideal defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; "makeProductRing" builds the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
- **IY** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a multi-homogeneous ideal defining a smooth complete intersection in \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; "makeProductRing" builds the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.

## Returns
intProd, a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md), a class in the Chow ring A of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} representing the Fulton-MacPherson intersection product of X with V in Y (where X is the scheme associated to IX, etc.).

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`intersectionProduct(Ideal,Ideal,Ideal)`](#intersectionproductidealidealideal)
- [`intersectionProduct(Ideal,Ideal,Ideal,QuotientRing)`](#intersectionproductidealidealidealquotientring)

