# segreDimX
This method computes the dimension X part of the Segre class of a scheme X inside a scheme Y, where X,Y are subschemes of some product of projective spaces

- **Package:** [SegreClasses](../../SegreClasses/package/SegreClasses.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SegreClasses.m2:128:8-128:17`
- **Result type:** [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md)
- **Aliases:** `SegreClasses$segreDimX`

## Description
For subschemes X, Y of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m} this command computes the dimension X part of the Segre class s(X, Y) of X in Y as a class in the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. This is faster than computing the entire Segre class.

## Parameters
- **A** — a [QuotientRing](../../Core/type/QuotientRing.md), the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}. This ring can be built by applying "makeChowRing" to the coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
- **IX** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a multi-homogeneous ideal defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; "makeProductRing" builds the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.
- **IY** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), a multi-homogeneous ideal defining a closed subscheme of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}; "makeProductRing" builds the graded coordinate ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.

## Returns
s, a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md), the dimension X part of the Segre class of the subscheme X defined by IX in the subscheme Y defined by IY as a class in the Chow ring of \PP^{n_1}x...x\PP^{n_m}.

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`segreDimX(Ideal,Ideal,QuotientRing)`](#segredimxidealidealquotientring)

## Examples
