# serialize
Reversible conversion of all Macaulay2 objects to strings

- **Package:** [Serialization](../../Serialization/package/Serialization.md)
- **Class:** [FunctionClosure](../../Core/type/FunctionClosure.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Serialization.m2:36:12-227:12`
- **Result type:** [String](../../Core/type/String.md)
- **Aliases:** `Serialization$serialize`

## Description
A convenient thing to serialize is the list of all user symbols provided by [userSymbols](../../Core/function/userSymbols.md), as in the following example.

## Parameters
- **x** — a [Thing](../../Core/type/Thing.md),

## Returns
a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), which when evaluated, will recreate the object x. The string can be written to a file, and "load" can be used to evaluate it later in another Macaulay2 session. Symbols encountered will have their values restored.

## Examples
