# connectedComponents
Find the connected components of an abstract simplicial complex

- **Package:** [SimplicialComplexes](../../SimplicialComplexes/package/SimplicialComplexes.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SimplicialComplexes/Code.m2:476:0-476:19`
- **Result type:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Aliases:** `SimplicialComplexes$connectedComponents`

## Description
Two vertices $v$ and $w$ in $\Delta$ are connected if there is a sequence of facets $F_0, F_1, \ldots, F_k \in \Delta$ such that $v \in F_0$, $w \in F_k$ and $F_i \cap F_{i+1} \neq \varnothing$ for all $1 \leq i \leq k-1$. A connected component of $\Delta$ is a maximal subcomplex of $\Delta$ in which all pairs of vertices are connected.

Our first example is an abstract simplicial complex with two connected components.

The void and irrelevant complexes each have one connected component.

## Parameters
- **Delta** — an "abstract simplicial complex",

## Returns
a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), of induced subcomplexes of $\Delta$, each one a distinct connected component of $\Delta$.

## Methods
- [`connectedComponents(HyperGraph)`](#connectedcomponentshypergraph)
- [`connectedComponents(Graph)`](#connectedcomponentsgraph)
- [`connectedComponents(Poset)`](#connectedcomponentsposet)
- [`connectedComponents(SimplicialComplex)`](#connectedcomponentssimplicialcomplex)

## Examples
