# slackIdeal
Computes the slack ideal

- **Package:** [SlackIdeals](../../SlackIdeals/package/SlackIdeals.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SlackIdeals.m2:661:0-661:10`
- **Result type:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md)
- **Aliases:** `SlackIdeals$slackIdeal`

## Description
The slack ideal of a d-polytope or rank d+1 matroid is the ideal of (d+2)-minors of its symbolic slack matrix, saturated by the product of the variables in the matrix.

If a list of points is given it can be treated as the vertices of a polytope, the ground set of a matroid or the facets of an abstract polytope by specifying the option [Object](../../SlackIdeals/symbol/Object.md). The default is as a polytope.

## Parameters
- **C** — a [Cone](../../Polyhedra/type/Cone.md), a cone
- **d** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the dimension of the polytope or 1 less than the rank of the matroid
- **M** — a "matroid", a matroid
- **P** — a [Polyhedron](../../Polyhedra/type/Polyhedron.md), a polytope
- **S** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a (symbolic) slack matrix
- **V** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), a list of vertices of a polytope, the vectors of a linear matroid, or facet sets of an abstract polytope

## Returns
I, an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), the slack ideal - the saturated ideal of (d+2)-minors of the symbolic slack matrix

## Options
- **[Object](../../SlackIdeals/symbol/Object.md)** — specify combinatorial object (default: `polytope`)
- **[Strategy](../../Core/symbol/Strategy.md)** — specifies saturation strategy to be used (default: `Eliminate`)
- **[CoefficientRing](../../Core/symbol/CoefficientRing.md)** — specifies the coefficient ring of the underlying ring of the ideal (default: `QQ`)
- **[Vars](../../SlackIdeals/symbol/Vars.md)** — specifies the variables to use to create the underlying ring of the ideal (default: `{}`)
- **[Saturate](../../SlackIdeals/symbol/Saturate.md)** — specifies saturation strategy to be used (default: `all`)

## Methods
- [`slackIdeal(ZZ,List)`](#slackidealzzlist)
- [`slackIdeal(Matroid)`](#slackidealmatroid)
- [`slackIdeal(Polyhedron)`](#slackidealpolyhedron)
- [`slackIdeal(Cone)`](#slackidealcone)
- [`slackIdeal(List)`](#slackideallist)
- [`slackIdeal(ZZ,Matrix)`](#slackidealzzmatrix)
- [`slackIdeal(Matrix)`](#slackidealmatrix)

## Examples
```macaulay2
V = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}};
```

```macaulay2
I = slackIdeal V
Order of vertices is 
{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}
```

```
o2 = ideal(x x x x  - x x x x )
            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7
o2 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]
                  0   7
```

```macaulay2
V = {{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}, {0, 1}};
```

```macaulay2
IP = slackIdeal V
Order of vertices is 
{{0, 0}, {1, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 1}}
```

```
o4 = ideal(x x x x  - x x x x )
            0 3 5 6    1 2 4 7
o4 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]
                  0   7
```

```macaulay2
IM = slackIdeal(V, Object => "matroid")
```

```
o5 = ideal (x x x   + x x x  , x x x  + x x x  , x x x  + x x x  , x x x  +
             4 8 10    5 7 11   1 8 9    2 6 11   0 5 9    2 3 10   0 4 6  
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     x x x , x x x x   - x x x x  , x x x x  - x x x x  , x x x x  -
      1 3 7   1 3 8 10    0 5 6 11   0 4 8 9    2 3 7 11   1 5 7 9  
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     x x x x  )
      2 4 6 10
o5 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x  ]
                  0   11
```

