# dgTable
Prints the table of (degree,genus) pairs

- **Package:** [SpaceCurves](../../SpaceCurves/package/SpaceCurves.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpaceCurves.m2:578:0-578:7`
- **Aliases:** `SpaceCurves$dgTable`

## Description
`dgTable` prints the table of (degree, genus) pairs, where the horizontal axis is the degree and the vertical is the genus. The input can be a [List](../../Core/type/List.md) of [Divisor](../../SpaceCurves/type/Divisor.md), [Curve](../../SpaceCurves/type/Curve.md), `PostulationChar` or [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md).

## Methods
- [`dgTable(List)`](#dgtablelist)

## Source
```m2
dgTable = method()
```

## Method details
### `dgTable(List)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpaceCurves.m2:579:16-610:1`
- **Domain:** [List](../../Core/type/List.md)

#### Source
```m2
dgTable List := L ->(
    --Takes a list of AbstractDivisors or RealizedDivisors
    --returns a (degree, genus) occurrence matrix    
    Ldg := apply(L, C -> (lift(degree C,ZZ), lift(genus C,ZZ)));
    dmax := max apply(Ldg,dg->first dg);
    dmin := min apply(Ldg,dg->first dg);
    gmax := max apply(Ldg,dg->last dg);
    gmin := min apply(Ldg,dg->last dg);
    M := mutableMatrix map(ZZ^(gmax-gmin+1),ZZ^(dmax-dmin+1),0);
    for dg in Ldg do (
	j := first dg - dmin;
	i := gmax - last dg;
    	M_(i,j) = M_(i,j)+1;		
    );
    yaxis := reverse splice{gmin..gmax};
    xaxis := toString splice{dmin..dmax};
    xaxis = replace(" ([0-9]),", "  \\1", replace("\\{", "g/d| ", replace("\\}", "", xaxis)));
    S := toString(transpose matrix{yaxis} | matrix M) | "\n";
    S = replace("matrix ", "", replace("\\{\\{", "{", replace("\\}\\}", "", S)));
    S = replace("\\}, ","\n", S);
    S = replace("\\{([0-9]+)", "\\1 |", S);
    S = replace(" ([0-9]),", "  \\1,", S);
    S = replace(",","",S);
    S = replace("\n([0-9]) ", "\n \\1 ", S);
    S = replace(" ([0-9])\n", "  \\1\n", S);
    S = replace("  0", "  .", S);
    S = net substring(S, 0, #S-1);
    xaxisbar := "---+";
    for i from 4 to width S do xaxisbar = xaxisbar | "-";
    S || xaxisbar || replace(",", "", xaxis)
    --transpose matrix{yaxis} | (matrix M || matrix{xaxis})
)
```

