# characterTable
Returns the character table of the symmetric group

- **Package:** [SpechtModule](../../SpechtModule/package/SpechtModule.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpechtModule.m2:91:0-91:14`
- **Result type:** [CharacterTable](../../SpechtModule/type/CharacterTable.md)
- **Aliases:** `SpechtModule$characterTable`

## Description
This method construct the irreducible characters of $S_n$. The method works by recursively calculating the character tables for the permutation modules of $S_n$. Then applying Gram-Schimdt algorithm to this characters using the inner product of characters we obtain the irreducible characters of $S_n$

## Parameters
- **n** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), the degree of the symmetric group

## Returns
an instance of the type "CharacterTable", the character table with the irreducible characters of $S_n$ indexed by partitions

## Methods
- [`characterTable(ZZ)`](#charactertablezz)

## Source
```m2
characterTable = method(TypicalValue => CharacterTable)
```

## Method details
### `characterTable(ZZ)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpechtModule.m2:92:21-120:1`
- **Domain:** [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md)
- **Returns:** [CharacterTable](../../SpechtModule/type/CharacterTable.md) (common typical value)

#### Source
```m2
characterTable ZZ := n -> (

    charTables := new MutableHashTable;




    for i from 1 to n do (


	charTable := new CharacterTable;
	partis := partitions i;
	charTable#index = hashTable apply(#partis, i-> partis#i => i);
    	charTable#length = #(partis);
    	charTable#degree = i;
    	charTable#values = mutableMatrix(ZZ,charTable#length,charTable#length);
    	charTables#i = charTable;
	y:= partitions(i);
	for j  to #y-1 do (

	    for k from j to #y-1 do (
		val:= calculateNumberOfEquals(y#(j),y#(k),charTables);
		(charTables#i)_(j,k)=val;
	    );
	);
    ); 
   charTable := reduceCharacterTable(charTables#n);
   charTable
)
```

