# GMtables
Make examples of reducible subschemes of P^5

- **Package:** [SpecialFanoFourfolds](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/package/SpecialFanoFourfolds.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpecialFanoFourfolds/GushelMukai.m2:117:94-117:102`
- **Aliases:** `SpecialFanoFourfolds$GMtables`

## Description
The corresponding example of fourfold reported in Table 1 of the aforementioned paper can be obtained as follows.

This is basically the same as doing this:

## Parameters
- **i** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), an integer between 1 and 21
- **K** — a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), the coefficient ring

## Returns
a triple of "varieties", $(B,V,C)$, which represents a reducible subscheme of $\mathbb{P}^5$, in accordance with the 21 examples listed in Table 2 of the paper On some families of Gushel-Mukai fourfolds (see https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.07026 ).

## Options
- **[Verify](../../Core/symbol/Verify.md)** (default: `true`)

## Methods
- [`GMtables(ZZ,Ring)`](#gmtableszzring)
- [`GMtables(Ring,String)`](#gmtablesringstring)
- [`GMtables(ZZ)`](#gmtableszz)
- [`GMtables(EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,EmbeddedProjectiveVariety)`](#gmtablesembeddedprojectivevarietyembeddedprojectivevarietyembeddedprojectivevariety)

## Examples
```macaulay2
(B,V,C) := GMtables(1,ZZ/33331)
```

```
o1 = (surface in PP^5 cut out by 4 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^1 2^3 , surface
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     in PP^5 cut out by 3 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^2 2^1 , curve in PP^5
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     cut out by 4 hypersurfaces of degrees 1^3 2^1 )
o1 : Sequence
```

```macaulay2
B * V == C
```

```
o2 = true
```

```macaulay2
psi = rationalMap(ideal B,Dominant=>2);
```

```
o3 : RationalMap (quadratic rational map from PP^5 to 5-dimensional subvariety of PP^8)
```

```macaulay2
X = gushelMukaiFourfold psi ideal V;
```

```
o4 : ProjectiveVariety, GM fourfold containing a surface of degree 2 and sectional genus 0
```

```macaulay2
gushelMukaiFourfold("1",ZZ/33331);
```

```
o5 : ProjectiveVariety, GM fourfold containing a surface of degree 2 and sectional genus 0
```

