# beauvilleMap
Construction of Beauville for complete intersections of three quadrics in P^7

- **Package:** [SpecialFanoFourfolds](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/package/SpecialFanoFourfolds.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunction](../../Core/type/MethodFunction.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpecialFanoFourfolds/IntersectionOfThreeQuadrics.m2:72:0-72:12`
- **Aliases:** `SpecialFanoFourfolds$beauvilleMap`

## Description
Smooth intersections of three quadrics in $\mathbb{P}^7$ are birational to quadric surface bundles over $\mathbb{P}^2$ with discriminant curve of degree 8. This is a construction of Beauville; see e.g. Proposition 6 in the paper [Intersections of three quadrics in P7](https://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/sdg/2017/0022/0001/SDG-2017-0022-0001-a009.pdf), by B. Hassett, A. Pirutka, and Y. Tschinkel.

## Parameters
- **X** — a "complete intersection of three quadrics in PP^7"

## Returns
f, a "multi-rational map", a birational map from $X$ to a fourfold $Y\subset\mathbb{P}^2\times\mathbb{P}^5$ whose first projection $Y\to\mathbb{P}^2$ is a quadric surface bundle

## Methods
- [`beauvilleMap(IntersectionOfThreeQuadricsInP7)`](#beauvillemapintersectionofthreequadricsinp7)

## Examples
```macaulay2
X = specialFourfold random({5:{1}},0_(PP_(ZZ/33331)^7));
```

```
o1 : ProjectiveVariety, complete intersection of three quadrics in PP^7 containing a surface of degree 1 and sectional genus 0
```

```macaulay2
f = beauvilleMap X;
```

```
o2 : MultirationalMap (birational map from X to 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^2 x PP^5)
```

```macaulay2
Y = target f;
```

```
o3 : ProjectiveVariety, 4-dimensional subvariety of PP^2 x PP^5
```

```macaulay2
inverse f;
```

```
o4 : MultirationalMap (birational map from Y to X)
```

```macaulay2
first projectionMaps target f;
```

```
o5 : QuadricFibration (dominant rational map from Y to PP^2)
```

## Source
```m2
beauvilleMap = method();
```

