# cubicFourfold
Make a special cubic fourfold

- **Package:** [SpecialFanoFourfolds](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/package/SpecialFanoFourfolds.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpecialFanoFourfolds/HodgeSpecialFourfolds.m2:46:98-46:111`
- **Result type:** [CubicFourfold](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/type/CubicFourfold.md)
- **Aliases:** `SpecialFanoFourfolds$cubicFourfold`

## Description
In the example below, we define a cubic fourfold containing a rational scroll of degree 7 with 3 nodes.

## Parameters
- **S** — an "embedded projective variety", an irreducible surface $S\subset\mathbb{P}^5$, which has as singularities only a finite number $n\geq 0$ of non-normal nodes (this number $n$ should be passed with the option NumNodes, otherwise it is obtained using a probabilistic method)
- **X** — an "embedded projective variety", a smooth cubic fourfold $X\subset \mathbb{P}^5$ containing the surface $S$

## Returns
a "cubic fourfold", the special cubic fourfold corresponding to the pair $(S,X)$

## Options
- **[NumNodes](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/symbol/NumNodes.md)**
- **[InputCheck](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/symbol/InputCheck.md)** (default: `1`)
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
