# gushelMukaiFourfold
Make a special Gushel-Mukai fourfold

- **Package:** [SpecialFanoFourfolds](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/package/SpecialFanoFourfolds.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/SpecialFanoFourfolds/HodgeSpecialFourfolds.m2:47:99-47:118`
- **Result type:** [GushelMukaiFourfold](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/type/GushelMukaiFourfold.md)
- **Aliases:** `SpecialFanoFourfolds$gushelMukaiFourfold`

## Description
In the following example, we define a Gushel-Mukai fourfold containing a so-called $\tau$-quadric.

## Parameters
- **S** — an "embedded projective variety", a smooth irreducible surface $S\subset\mathbb{P}^8$
- **X** — an "embedded projective variety", a smooth prime Fano fourfold $X\subset \mathbb{P}^8$ of degree 10 and sectional genus 6, which contains the surface $S$

## Returns
a "Gushel-Mukai fourfold", the special Gushel-Mukai fourfold corresponding to the pair $(S,X)$

## Options
- **[InputCheck](../../SpecialFanoFourfolds/symbol/InputCheck.md)** (default: `1`)
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`gushelMukaiFourfold(EmbeddedProjectiveVariety,EmbeddedProjectiveVariety)`](#gushelmukaifourfoldembeddedprojectivevarietyembeddedprojectivevariety)
