- **Aliases:** `SpecialFanoFourfolds$trisecantFlop`

## Description
This function requires the package [TrisecantFlops](https://github.com/giovannistagliano/TrisecantFlops). If not present the user will be asked to automatically install the package.

## Parameters
- **i** — an [ZZ](../../Core/type/ZZ.md), an integer between 0 and 17

## Returns
the i-th example of birational map $X\dashrightarrow W$ in accordance to the Table 1 in the paper Trisecant Flops, their associated K3 surfaces and the rationality of some Fano fourfolds (see https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.01263 ).

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `false`)

## Methods
- [`trisecantFlop(ZZ)`](#trisecantflopzz)

## Source
```m2
trisecantFlop = method(Options => {Verbose => false});
```

## Method details
