# tLastMon
Give the last t-spread monomial of the Borel shadow a given t-spread monomial

- **Package:** [TSpreadIdeals](../../TSpreadIdeals/package/TSpreadIdeals.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/TSpreadIdeals.m2:62:0-62:8`
- **Result type:** [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md)
- **Aliases:** `TSpreadIdeals$tLastMon`

## Description
The function `tLastMon(u, gap, t)` gives the smallest `t`-spread monomials of the Borel shadow iterated `gap`times of `u`, that is, the smallest monomial of $B_\texttt{t}\{\texttt{u}\}$, with respect to $>_\mathrm{slex}.$If `MaxInd` is greater than -1 the function `tLastMon(u, gap, t, MaxInd=>m)` gives the smallest `t`-spread monomial for which the maximum of the support is `m`The Borel shadow of a `t`-spread monomial `u`, is defined as the shadow of the strongly stable set generated by `u`. To work in a `t`-spread contest, the Borel shadow of `u` is the `t`-shadow of $B_\texttt{t}\{u\}$. Examples:

## Parameters
- **gap** — a positive integer representing the difference between the degrees
- **t** — a positive integer that identifies the t-spread contest
- **u** — a t-spread monomial of a polynomial ring

## Returns
a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md), the smallest t-spread monomial of the Borel shadow of u, with respect to lexcografic order

## Options
- **[MaxInd](../../TSpreadIdeals/symbol/MaxInd.md)** (default: `-1`)

## Methods
- [`tLastMon(RingElement,ZZ,ZZ)`](#tlastmonringelementzzzz)

## Examples
