# beilinson
Apply the beilinson functor

- **Package:** [TateOnProducts](../../TateOnProducts/package/TateOnProducts.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/TateOnProducts.m2:1525:0-1525:9`
- **Aliases:** `TateOnProducts$beilinson`

## Description
The Beilinson functor is a functor from the category of free E-modules to the category of coherent sheaves which associates to a cyclic free E-module of generated in multidegree a the vector bundle U^a. Note that the U^a for multidegrees a=\{a_1,..., a_t\} with 0 \le a_i \le n_i form a full exceptional series for the derived category of coherent sheaves on the product PP = P^{n_1} \times ... \times P^{n_t} of t projective spaces, see e.g. [Tate Resolutions on Products of Projective Spaces](http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.5724).

In the function we compute from a complex of free E-modules the corresponding complex of graded S-modules, whose sheafifications are the corresponding sheaves. The corresponding graded S-module are chosen as quotients of free S-modules in case of the default option BundleType=>PrunedQuotient, or as submodules of free S-modules. The true Beilinson functor is obtained by the sheafication of resulting the complex.

The Beilinson monad of a coherent sheaf $\mathcal F$ is the sheafication of beilinson( T($\mathcal F$)) of its Tate resolution T($\mathcal F$).

## Parameters
- **F** — a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), a free module over the exterior algebra E
- **psi** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a map between free modules over E
- **T** — a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), a complex of free modules over E

## Returns
M, a [Module](../../Core/type/Module.md), a module over the symmetric algebra S; phi, a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), a map between S-modules; C, a [Complex](../../SRdeformations/type/Complex.md), a chain complex of S-modules

## Options
- **[BundleType](../../TateOnProducts/symbol/BundleType.md)** (default: `PrunedQuotient`)

## Methods
- [`beilinson(Module)`](#beilinsonmodule)
- [`beilinson(Matrix)`](#beilinsonmatrix)
- [`beilinson(Complex)`](#beilinsoncomplex)

