# testIdeal
Compute a test ideal in a Q-Gorenstein ring

- **Package:** [TestIdeals](../../TestIdeals/package/TestIdeals.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/TestIdeals/testIdeals.m2:77:0-77:9`
- **Result type:** [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md)
- **Aliases:** `TestIdeals$testIdeal`

## Description
Given a normal $\mathbb{Q}$-Gorenstein ring $R$, `testIdeal(R)` simply computes the test ideal `\tau`($R$).

Given a nonnegative rational number $t$ and an element $f$ of a normal $\mathbb{Q}$-Gorenstein ring $R$, `testIdeal(t, f)` computes the test ideal `\tau`($R$, $f^{ t}$).

The ring $R$ need not be a polynomial ring, as the next example illustrates.

Given nonnegative rational numbers $t_1, t_2, \ldots$ and ring elements $f_1, f_2, \ldots$, `testIdeal(\{t_1, t_2,\ldots\},\{f_1, f_2,\ldots\})` computes the test ideal `\tau`($R$, $f_1^{t_1} f_2^{t_2}\cdots$).

It is often more efficient to pass a list, as opposed to finding a common denominator and passing a single element, since `testIdeal` can do things in a more intelligent way for such a list.

The option `AssumeDomain` (default value `false`) is used when finding a test element. The option `FrobeniusRootStrategy` (default value `Substitution`) is passed to internal [frobeniusRoot](../../TestIdeals/methodFunction/frobeniusRoot.md) calls.

When working in a $\mathbb{Q}$-Gorenstein ring $R$, `testIdeal` looks for a positive integer $N$ such that $N K_R$ is Cartier. The option `MaxCartierIndex` (default value $10$) controls the maximum value of $N$ to consider in this search. If the smallest such $N$ turns out to be greater than the value passed to `MaxCartierIndex`, then `testIdeal` returns an error.

The $\mathbb{Q}$-Gorenstein index can be specified by the user through the option `QGorensteinIndex`; when this option is used, the search for $N$ is bypassed, and the option `MaxCartierIndex` ignored.

## Parameters
- **f** — a [RingElement](../../Core/type/RingElement.md), the element in a pair
- **fList** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), consisting of ring elements f_1,\ldots,f_n, for a pair
- **R** — a [Ring](../../Core/type/Ring.md), a $\mathbb{Q}$-Gorenstein ring
- **t** — a [Number](../../Core/type/Number.md), the formal exponent to which f is raised
- **tList** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md), consisting of formal exponents t_1,\ldots,t_n for the elements of fList

## Returns
an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), the test ideal \tau(R), \tau(R,f^{t}), or \tau(R,f_1^{t_1}\ldots f_n^{t_n}), depending on the arguments passed

## Options
- **[MaxCartierIndex](../../TestIdeals/symbol/MaxCartierIndex.md)** (default: `10`)
- **[FrobeniusRootStrategy](../../TestIdeals/symbol/FrobeniusRootStrategy.md)** (default: `Substitution`)
- **[QGorensteinIndex](../../TestIdeals/symbol/QGorensteinIndex.md)** (default: `0`)
- **[AssumeDomain](../../TestIdeals/symbol/AssumeDomain.md)** (default: `false`)

