# topcomIsTriangulation
Determine if a set of subsets is a triangulation of a point set

- **Package:** [Topcom](../../Topcom/package/Topcom.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Topcom.m2:329:0-329:21`
- **Result type:** [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md)
- **Aliases:** `Topcom$topcomIsTriangulation`

## Description
#### Caveat
topcom doesn't check that the subsets given are simplices, so we do that directly.

## Parameters
- **A** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md),
- **tri** — a [List](../../Core/type/List.md),

## Returns
a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md),

## Options
- **[Homogenize](../../Topcom/symbol/Homogenize.md)** (default: `true`)

## Methods
- [`topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix,List)`](#topcomistriangulationmatrixlist)

## Source
```m2
topcomIsTriangulation = method(Options => {Homogenize => true});
```

## Method details
### `topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix,List)`
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/Topcom.m2:330:50-347:1`
- **Domain:** [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), [List](../../Core/type/List.md)
- **Returns:** [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md) (this method)

#### Source
```m2
topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix, List) := Boolean => opts -> (Vin, T) -> (
   -- Topcom does not check whether the sets in T actually form simplices. In
   -- that case it throws an error instead of giving an answer.  -- So we do it
   -- manually:
   V := if opts.Homogenize then promote(augment Vin, QQ) else promote(Vin, QQ);
   d := numRows V;
   if not all(T, t-> #t == d) then (
      << "Index sets do not correspond to full-dimensional simplices" << endl;
      return false;
   );
   simplices := apply(T, t -> V_t);
   if not all(simplices, s->d==rank s) then (
      << "Index sets do not correspond to full-dimensional simplices" << endl;
      return false;
   );
   (outfile, errfile) := callTopcom("points2nflips --checktriang -v", {topcomPoints(V, Homogenize=>false), [], T });
   not match("not valid", get errfile)
)
```

