# solvingFlatteningRelations
Solving the flatttening relations over QQ

- **Package:** [WeierstrassSemigroups](../../WeierstrassSemigroups/package/WeierstrassSemigroups.md)
- **Class:** [MethodFunctionWithOptions](../../Core/type/MethodFunctionWithOptions.md)
- **Protected:** true
- **Mutable:** false
- **Defined at:** `/home/flux/.cache/yay/macaulay2/src/M2/M2/Macaulay2/packages/WeierstrassSemigroups.m2:220:32-220:58`
- **Aliases:** `WeierstrassSemigroups$solvingFlatteningRelations`

## Description
We look for subsets of the source consisting of all but codim base many elements which define a linear subspace of the base. Substituting random small values for these variables, might lead to an ideal which defines a point in the base. There is some intermediate output.

## Parameters
- **base** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), irreducible ideal of flattening relations
- **family** — a [Matrix](../../Core/type/Matrix.md), matrix of generators of the family
- **I** — an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), semigroup ideal

## Returns
worked, a [Boolean](../../Core/type/Boolean.md), true if a smoothing family was found; fiber, an [Ideal](../../Core/type/Ideal.md), ideal of a 1-parameter smoothing family

## Options
- **[Verbose](../../Core/symbol/Verbose.md)** (default: `0`)
- **[BaseField](../../WeierstrassSemigroups/symbol/BaseField.md)** (default: `ZZ/10000019`)
- **[CoeffSize](../../WeierstrassSemigroups/symbol/CoeffSize.md)** (default: `1`)
- **[CoeffBound](../../WeierstrassSemigroups/symbol/CoeffBound.md)** (default: `10000`)

